{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":8920,"output":7825,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6270,"totalTokens":16745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me analyze each item.\n\nQ021: source: \"which you do not understand: #{italic}#...\" target: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：...\" Source says \"which you do not understand\" — target says \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" (\"even if you know this language, you cannot understand\"). That's a negation flip. Source: you do not understand. Target: even if you know this language, you cannot understand. Hmm, source_context: the lore branch when player does NOT speak shertul shows \"which you do not understand:\" followed by the untranslated text; when speaks_shertul, shows translation. The source string is the \"which you do not understand\" variant. Target adds \"即使你懂得这种语言\" — actually this inverts: source states player doesn't understand; target says even if you know the language you cannot understand. This is a negation/condition defect. FINDING, CONDITION or STATE. Evidence: \"which you do not understand\". target_span: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". Correction: \"你看不懂：\" or similar. Actually source says \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand\" — the text underneath which you do not understand. Correction: \"下面有一些你看不懂的文字：\". FINDING, CONDITION (negation flipped). Claim_type: CONDITION or STATE. Use CONDITION.\n\nWait—but the source_context shows the two branches: untranslated text shown when player does NOT speak shertul, translated when does. The target's \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" contradicts: source's branch shows the untranslated string precisely because you don't understand. Actually target says even if you know the language you can't understand it — the string \"Sho ch'zun...\" is shertul language, untranslated. In source, \"which you do not understand\" is the correct meaning. Target changes to \"even if you understand this language, you cannot understand\" — flip. FINDING.\n\nQ022: source: \"The staff will allow us to drain...\" target: \"这根法杖将让我们得以...\" OK. Source context has \"The staff has allowed us\" but the source given says \"will allow\". Translation matches source \"will allow\" — 将让我们得以. Fine. Also last line: \"You cannot stop us now!\" → \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — \"You cannot stop us now\" means \"你们现在无法阻止我们\" (you are unable to stop us). Target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了\" — same meaning. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ023: source: \"What do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\" target: \"你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\" Fine. The italic part: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" → \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\" — \"peer out\" = 向外窥视/望出来. Target says \"凝视着他\" — at him? Source doesn't specify object. \"peer out\" — looking out through the slot. \"凝视着他\" adds \"him\" — could be the NPC peering out at the player. Minor addition but compatible with context (the NPC peers out at the player who's at the door). \"gaze at him\" — the player is the one addressed; the eyes peer out at... the player. But target uses \"他\" (him) while the addressee is the player (\"你\"). Also \"A slot in the door opens\" → \"门上开了一个小洞\" — slot = 狭缝/小口, \"小洞\" is a hole, minor. \"凝视着他\" vs \"向外窥视\" — the pronoun 他 refers to whom? If the eyes belong to the doorkeeper, they peer out at the player, so should be \"你\" or just \"向外张望\". Is this an objective defect? The \"him\" as referent is wrong-ish—the addressee is the player addressed as \"你\". But it could refer to a third person present. Hmm. It's a mild referent issue. I'd report as UNCERTAIN maybe. Actually rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence isn't a defect. The peering is at whoever is at the door; in the dialog the player. Using 他 while addressing 你 is inconsistent but possibly a translation convention. I'll report UNCERTAIN for REFERENT? Or skip. Also \"peer out\" means to look out from within; \"凝视着他\" adds a direction. I think it's low severity; I might report UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Hmm, let me be careful about false positives. The main sentence is fine. I'll leave candidates empty for Q023? The \"他\" is the most questionable. The dialog is between NPC and player; eyes peer out and look at the player (\"你\"). Translating as \"他\" introduces third-person referent not in source. I'd report as FINDING? It's fairly subjective. I'll do UNCERTAIN with REFERENT.\n\nQ024: \"Aeryn, are you well?\" → \"艾琳，你还好么？\" Fine. No defect.\n\nQ025: source: \"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\" target: \"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\" Fine. \"orbs of command\" → 指令水晶球 — okay, orb = 球. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ026: \"Number of items to make\" → \"制作的物品数量\" Fine.\n\nQ027: source: \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" target: \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Hmm \"and I'll have everything prepared\" — future: \"我就会把一切都准备好\". Target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" adds certainty, and \"准备好了\" perfective. Minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" = 届时我会把一切都准备好. Target is close. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will surely have everything ready\" — acceptable. Second: \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago.\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。\" Fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\" — \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\" — our attempt to create the portal / portal attempt. Target says \"你通过传送门时\" (when you pass through the portal). Source: \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt at the portal (creating/opening portal). Hmm — \"surviving our portal attempt\" — could be surviving the attempt to open the portal. Target shifts to surviving passing through the portal. Is that a defect? \"our portal attempt\" is ambiguous; the risk is during the portal creation/travel. The target changes \"our\" to \"你\" and \"attempt\" to \"通过传送门时\". This changes subject: our attempt → your passing through. I'd report as FINDING? It's arguably ambiguous. \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt involving the portal they will create for the player. \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\" = your odds of surviving when you go through the portal. Source: your odds of surviving our attempt at the portal. These differ: whose action. \"our\" vs \"your\". I'd report FINDING with SUBJECT/OTHER? Or UNCERTAIN. Hmm. The safest: report UNCERTAIN with claim OTHER or SUBJECT. Evidence: \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\". target_span: \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Correction: \"我们尝试开启传送门时你存活的几率\" or \"你在我们尝试传送时存活的几率\". I'll mark FINDING? The change of \"our\" to \"你\" is objective. But \"portal attempt\" could mean \"attempt to use the portal\" — still \"our attempt\". The target removes \"our\". I'll do UNCERTAIN.\n\nActually also \"Return in a few days\" — 几天后你回来 fine.\n\nQ028: source: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" fine. \"The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\" fine. \"You must go there and find the source.\" → \"你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\" \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — minor addition, compatible. Fine.\n\nQ029: source: \"Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain\" → \"探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽\" fine. \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" Hmm — \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" means: so far we've only encountered hatchlings (nothing but = only). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings — that's the OPPOSITE! Source: only hatchlings (no adult dragons). Target: never met hatchlings. That's a clear negation flip / value error. FINDING. Evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" target_span: \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\"。 Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到过幼龙\". Claim_type: OTHER or VALUE/STATE. Use STATE? It's about what they've encountered. I'd use VALUE or STATE. Let's use STATE.\n\nWait — could \"Nothing but hatchlings\" mean \"nothing except hatchlings\" i.e., only hatchlings so far — yes. And the rest: \"if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon\" — consistent with only finding hatchlings (not enough dragonhide). Target \"从未遇上幼龙\" contradicts. Definitely FINDING.\n\nAlso \"Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know\" → \"高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人\" — \"money-grubbing\" included as 贪财, Thronesmen → 钢铁王座 (Throne). Fine. \"Xann\" → 希安. \"wyrmic\" → 龙战士 — wyrmic is a class; 龙战士 acceptable. \"if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\" → \"现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\" — \"draconic talents\" → 操控龙族力量的本事 — addition but compatible. Fine.\n\nSo Q029 has one FINDING.\n\nQ030: source: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — \"my\" is added; source is a menu action to report a user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" = report MY bad behavior — wrong direction! It should be \"举报不良行为\" (report [them] for bad behavior). Adding \"我的\" reverses the meaning. FINDING. Evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\". target_span \"举报我的不良行为\". Correction: \"举报不良行为\". Claim_type: SUBJECT or DIRECTION. Use SUBJECT? Or ADDITION. I'd say SUBJECT (who did bad behavior). Or DIRECTION. I'll use SUBJECT.\n\nQ031: source: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" ≠ \"丢弃\" (drop). The popup offers both inventory and drop options, so \"放置\" is correct; \"丢弃\" narrows to drop. FINDING. Evidence: \"Place the object where?\" target_span \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\". Claim_type: ACTION. Note source_context shows options include \"Inventory of %s\" and \"Drop @\" — supporting that place ≠ only drop. That context supports the finding.\n\nQ032: source: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" target: \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" — target adds \"在'龙之贪婪'成就中\". From source_context, the achievement with 3000 is \"Treasure Hoarder\"; Dragon's Greed is 8000. So the addition is wrong info — it attaches the desc to Dragon's Greed achievement, but 3000 corresponds to Treasure Hoarder. However, the rule: addition compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong by evidence? The context shows DRAGON_GREED desc = 8000. So adding \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" to a 3000 desc is contradicted by visible evidence. FINDING. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" for DRAGON_GREED, and the 3000 desc belongs to \"Treasure Hoarder\". Evidence must be verbatim from source_context: I can quote \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" and \"return who.money >= 3000\". Evidence string should be verbatim occurrence. I'll use: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" ... hmm evidence must be a single verbatim string. Use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — verbatim in context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` yes. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim_type: ADDITION.\n\nQ033: \"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\" → \"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\" Fine. Note in context this is \"Almost Master of Arena\" but translation only handles desc; fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite! \"let you down\" = 让你失望; \"I will NOT let you down\" = 我不会让你失望. Target says \"我一定会让你失望的\" = I will definitely disappoint you. FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"I will not let you down!\" Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\".\n\nQ035: source: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" target: \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20. FINDING, VALUE. Evidence: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" Correction: \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\"\n\nQ036: source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" target: \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" but compatible-ish. Source is an achievement name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — actually from context it's an achievement name for killing Linaniil. Adding \"发现\" — hmm, is that judgeable wrong? Source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" — \"这可真令人印象深刻！\" Target adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). The achievement is about a kill, not a discovery. But by visible evidence alone, \"this discovery\" is an addition that specifies the referent as a discovery. Is it \"compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong\"? The context desc: \"Killed Linaniil...\" — killing isn't a discovery. Hmm, achievements can be named loosely. I think this is a mild addition. Could report UNCERTAIN ADDITION. Actually rule: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" The evidence shows the achievement is for killing Linaniil — \"这个发现\" (this discovery) is arguably incompatible... but the exclamation could refer to anything. I lean UNCERTAIN or empty. Hmm. I'll report UNCERTAIN with ADDITION: target adds \"发现\" which is not in source; the source is a general exclamation. Actually is it worth reporting? It's a name; adding \"发现\" changes meaning somewhat. I'll include UNCERTAIN.\n\nHmm, but caution against over-reporting. The exclamation \"Now, this is impressive!\" in context of killing — the target invents a discovery. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: source: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" target: \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — \"power\" (力量) is omitted; \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" = 对力量与永生的狂热梦想. Target: \"成就你的野心\" (achieved your ambition) — \"power\" dropped, \"wild\" dropped. OMISSION of \"power\". Is it substantive? \"dreams of power and eternal life\" → 野心 covers dreams generally but loses \"power\". Also \"eternal life\" kept. Hmm — \"野心\" (ambition) loosely covers \"power and eternal life\" dreams? It only explicitly mentions eternal life. Omission of \"力量\". Report FINDING OMISSION? It's a partial omission; the meaning \"wild dreams of power\" is fairly significant for a Lichform achievement. I'd report FINDING OMISSION with evidence \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" and correction \"实现了你对力量与永生的狂想：你成为了巫妖！\". Or UNCERTAIN. \"野心\" does encompass desire for power arguably... but combined with only 永恒的生命 mentioned. I'll do FINDING? Hmm. Let me think: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — the target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\" reads as: achieved your ambition AND obtained eternal life. Actually that covers both power (ambition) and eternal life. \"野心\" ≈ ambition for power. It's a reasonable compression. I'd say no objective defect... but \"wild\" omitted, minor. I'll leave empty. Hmm, borderline. I'll leave empty candidates for Q037.\n\nQ038: source: \"Kickin' it old-school\" target: \"现代风格\" — completely opposite! \"old-school\" = 老派/复古; target says 现代风格 (modern style). FINDING, DIRECTION or VALUE. Evidence: \"Kickin' it old-school\". Correction: \"老派风格\" / \"怀旧复古\". Claim_type: DIRECTION (opposite meaning) or OTHER. Use DIRECTION? It's more VALUE (wrong style). I'll use OTHER or DIRECTION. \"old-school\" → modern is an antonym flip: DIRECTION.\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" — matches: the player (main) is dead and kills a boss (BOSS_REVENGE \"Take you with me\"). Fine. p.dead means the main party member is dead. Target fine.\n\nQ040: source: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" target: \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"maintain it in orbit\" = 维持其轨道运行; target says \"稳定在地面上\" (stabilize on the ground) — opposite/orbit omitted. Also \"Abashed Expanse\" translated as 次元浮岛 (a known translation? The zone is a floating shard). The key defect: \"in orbit\" → \"在地面上\". FINDING. Evidence: \"maintain it in orbit\". target_span: \"使其稳定在地面上\". Correction: \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\". Claim_type: VALUE or STATE. Use STATE? \"in orbit\" vs \"on the ground\" — VALUE/STATE. I'll use STATE.\n\nNow double-check Q022 for any issue: source \"The staff will allow us\" — context has \"has allowed\" for one branch; but source given is \"will allow\", target matches. Also \"You cannot stop us now!\" target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — good. Context's alternate has \"It is already too late...\" — not relevant. No findings for Q022.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ028: fine. Actually \"unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" — restless = 烦躁不安/躁动; 蠢蠢欲动 means about to move/start action — acceptable.\n\nQ030: confirm — the menu item is an action on another user in chat, \"Report for bad behavior\" — report that user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" says report my own bad behavior — wrong. FINDING.\n\nQ031: FINDING.\n\nQ034: FINDING.\n\nQ035: FINDING.\n\nQ038: FINDING.\n\nQ040: FINDING.\n\nQ021: FINDING.\n\nQ029: FINDING.\n\nQ032: FINDING.\n\nQ027: UNCERTAIN for \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\". Let me finalize. Also check \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" — \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads fine as future in Chinese (\"到时候肯定准备好了\"). OK.\n\nQ023: I'll include the UNCERTAIN REFERENT for \"凝视着他\". Hmm, actually reconsider: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" — peer out = 向外窥视. Target \"凝视着他\" — the \"他\" refers presumably to the player, but the next line addresses the player as \"你\". Within the same text, \"他\" would be confusing. But is this a \"客观、实质性\" defect? The peering direction and object are added. I'll include UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Evidence: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\". target_span: \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\"。\n\nActually wait — the player is @playerdescriptor.race@, being addressed. The eyes peer out at the player. Using 他 vs 你 — in Chinese game translations, third person for the player is odd but occurs. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ036: UNCERTAIN ADDITION: \"这个发现\" — the source is just an exclamation; the achievement (per context) is for killing Linaniil, not a discovery. I'll make it FINDING? Evidence: \"name = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"LINANIIL_DEAD\\\"\" and desc \"Killed Linaniil\" — but evidence field must be verbatim from source or source_context. I could use \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\" as evidence showing it's a kill not a discovery. Hmm, but the translation is of the name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — the name itself doesn't mention discovery. Adding \"这个发现\" specifies a referent that conflicts with the kill context. I'd say UNCERTAIN is safer. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\". Correction: \"这可真令人印象深刻！\". Verdict UNCERTAIN, claim ADDITION.\n\nHmm, actually reconsider whether to report Q036 at all. \"Now, this is impressive!\" as an achievement name for killing the Supreme Archmage — \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻\" — \"发现\" is a genuine addition not supported. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ027 finalize: UNCERTAIN, claim SUBJECT or OTHER. \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Changes \"our portal attempt\" (our attempt at the portal) to \"when you pass through the portal\". Whose action changed: our → your passing. I'd claim SUBJECT. target_span \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". evidence \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\". Correction: \"这能大大提高你在我们尝试开启传送门时的存活几率。\" Verdict: UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: decide. \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\". \"power\" — 野心 implies ambition which in context = power? Not explicit. \"wild\" omitted. Hmm. Two components: power + eternal life. Target: 野心 (ambition — could cover power) + 永恒的生命. I think this is a defensible compression; not an objective defect. Empty.\n\nActually wait, one more consideration for Q021: the target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" — could the translator have intended a different meaning from source? Source: \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand:\" — the translation flips it to \"even if you know this language, you cannot understand it\". Given source_context, the untranslated text is shown when the player does NOT speak shertul — so \"you do not understand\" is correct; target's version is a different claim. This is an objective change. FINDING, claim CONDITION (negation of condition). target_span \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". evidence \"which you do not understand\". Correction: \"下面是一些你看不懂的文字：\" — well the target only needs c