aff has allowed us\" but the source given says \"will allow\". Translation matches source \"will allow\" — 将让我们得以. Fine. Also last line: \"You cannot stop us now!\" → \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — \"You cannot stop us now\" means \"你们现在无法阻止我们\" (you are unable to stop us). Target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了\" — same meaning. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ023: source: \"What do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\" target: \"你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\" Fine. The italic part: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" → \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\" — \"peer out\" = 向外窥视/望出来. Target says \"凝视着他\" — at him? Source doesn't specify object. \"peer out\" — looking out through the slot. \"凝视着他\" adds \"him\" — could be the NPC peering out at the player. Minor addition but compatible with context (the NPC peers out at the player who's at the door). \"gaze at him\" — the player is the one addressed; the eyes peer out at... the player. But target uses \"他\" (him) while the addressee is the player (\"你\"). Also \"A slot in the door opens\" → \"门上开了一个小洞\" — slot = 狭缝/小口, \"小洞\" is a hole, minor. \"凝视着他\" vs \"向外窥视\" — the pronoun 他 refers to whom? If the eyes belong to the doorkeeper, they peer out at the player, so should be \"你\" or just \"向外张望\". Is this an objective defect? The \"him\" as referent is wrong-ish—the addressee is the player addressed as \"你\". But it could refer to a third person present. Hmm. It's a mild referent issue. I'd report as UNCERTAIN maybe. Actually rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence isn't a defect. The peering is at whoever is at the door; in the dialog the player. Using 他 while addressing 你 is inconsistent but possibly a translation convention. I'll report UNCERTAIN for REFERENT? Or skip. Also \"peer out\" means to look out from within; \"凝视着他\" adds a direction. I think it's low severity; I might report UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Hmm, let me be careful about false positives. The main sentence is fine. I'll leave candidates empty for Q023? The \"他\" is the most questionable. The dialog is between NPC and player; eyes peer out and look at the player (\"你\"). Translating as \"他\" introduces third-person referent not in source. I'd report as FINDING? It's fairly subjective. I'll do UNCERTAIN with REFERENT.\n\nQ024: \"Aeryn, are you well?\" → \"艾琳，你还好么？\" Fine. No defect.\n\nQ025: source: \"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\" target: \"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\" Fine. \"orbs of command\" → 指令水晶球 — okay, orb = 球. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ026: \"Number of items to make\" → \"制作的物品数量\" Fine.\n\nQ027: source: \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" target: \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Hmm \"and I'll have everything prepared\" — future: \"我就会把一切都准备好\". Target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" adds certainty, and \"准备好了\" perfective. Minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" = 届时我会把一切都准备好. Target is close. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will surely have everything ready\" — acceptable. Second: \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago.\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。\" Fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\" — \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\" — our attempt to create the portal / portal attempt. Target says \"你通过传送门时\" (when you pass through the portal). Source: \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt at the portal (creating/opening portal). Hmm — \"surviving our portal attempt\" — could be surviving the attempt to open the portal. Target shifts to surviving passing through the portal. Is that a defect? \"our portal attempt\" is ambiguous; the risk is during the portal creation/travel. The target changes \"our\" to \"你\" and \"attempt\" to \"通过传送门时\". This changes subject: our attempt → your passing through. I'd report as FINDING? It's arguably ambiguous. \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt involving the portal they will create for the player. \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\" = your odds of surviving when you go through the portal. Source: your odds of surviving our attempt at the portal. These differ: whose action. \"our\" vs \"your\". I'd report FINDING with SUBJECT/OTHER? Or UNCERTAIN. Hmm. The safest: report UNCERTAIN with claim OTHER or SUBJECT. Evidence: \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\". target_span: \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Correction: \"我们尝试开启传送门时你存活的几率\" or \"你在我们尝试传送时存活的几率\". I'll mark FINDING? The change of \"our\" to \"你\" is objective. But \"portal attempt\" could mean \"attempt to use the portal\" — still \"our attempt\". The target removes \"our\". I'll do UNCERTAIN.\n\nActually also \"Return in a few days\" — 几天后你回来 fine.\n\nQ028: source: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" fine. \"The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\" fine. \"You must go there and find the source.\" → \"你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\" \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — minor addition, compatible. Fine.\n\nQ029: source: \"Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain\" → \"探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽\" fine. \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" Hmm — \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" means: so far we've only encountered hatchlings (nothing but = only). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings — that's the OPPOSITE! Source: only hatchlings (no adult dragons). Target: never met hatchlings. That's a clear negation flip / value error. FINDING. Evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" target_span: \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\"。 Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到过幼龙\". Claim_type: OTHER or VALUE/STATE. Use STATE? It's about what they've encountered. I'd use VALUE or STATE. Let's use STATE.\n\nWait — could \"Nothing but hatchlings\" mean \"nothing except hatchlings\" i.e., only hatchlings so far — yes. And the rest: \"if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon\" — consistent with only finding hatchlings (not enough dragonhide). Target \"从未遇上幼龙\" contradicts. Definitely FINDING.\n\nAlso \"Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know\" → \"高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人\" — \"money-grubbing\" included as 贪财, Thronesmen → 钢铁王座 (Throne). Fine. \"Xann\" → 希安. \"wyrmic\" → 龙战士 — wyrmic is a class; 龙战士 acceptable. \"if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\" → \"现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\" — \"draconic talents\" → 操控龙族力量的本事 — addition but compatible. Fine.\n\nSo Q029 has one FINDING.\n\nQ030: source: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — \"my\" is added; source is a menu action to report a user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" = report MY bad behavior — wrong direction! It should be \"举报不良行为\" (report [them] for bad behavior). Adding \"我的\" reverses the meaning. FINDING. Evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\". target_span \"举报我的不良行为\". Correction: \"举报不良行为\". Claim_type: SUBJECT or DIRECTION. Use SUBJECT? Or ADDITION. I'd say SUBJECT (who did bad behavior). Or DIRECTION. I'll use SUBJECT.\n\nQ031: source: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" ≠ \"丢弃\" (drop). The popup offers both inventory and drop options, so \"放置\" is correct; \"丢弃\" narrows to drop. FINDING. Evidence: \"Place the object where?\" target_span \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\". Claim_type: ACTION. Note source_context shows options include \"Inventory of %s\" and \"Drop @\" — supporting that place ≠ only drop. That context supports the finding.\n\nQ032: source: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" target: \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" — target adds \"在'龙之贪婪'成就中\". From source_context, the achievement with 3000 is \"Treasure Hoarder\"; Dragon's Greed is 8000. So the addition is wrong info — it attaches the desc to Dragon's Greed achievement, but 3000 corresponds to Treasure Hoarder. However, the rule: addition compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong by evidence? The context shows DRAGON_GREED desc = 8000. So adding \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" to a 3000 desc is contradicted by visible evidence. FINDING. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" for DRAGON_GREED, and the 3000 desc belongs to \"Treasure Hoarder\". Evidence must be verbatim from source_context: I can quote \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" and \"return who.money >= 3000\". Evidence string should be verbatim occurrence. I'll use: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" ... hmm evidence must be a single verbatim string. Use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — verbatim in context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` yes. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim_type: ADDITION.\n\nQ033: \"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\" → \"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\" Fine. Note in context this is \"Almost Master of Arena\" but translation only handles desc; fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite! \"let you down\" = 让你失望; \"I will NOT let you down\" = 我不会让你失望. Target says \"我一定会让你失望的\" = I will definitely disappoint you. FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"I will not let you down!\" Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\".\n\nQ035: source: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" target: \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20. FINDING, VALUE. Evidence: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" Correction: \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\"\n\nQ036: source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" target: \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" but compatible-ish. Source is an achievement name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — actually from context it's an achievement name for killing Linaniil. Adding \"发现\" — hmm, is that judgeable wrong? Source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" — \"这可真令人印象深刻！\" Target adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). The achievement is about a kill, not a discovery. But by visible evidence alone, \"this discovery\" is an addition that specifies the referent as a discovery. Is it \"compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong\"? The context desc: \"Killed Linaniil...\" — killing isn't a discovery. Hmm, achievements can be named loosely. I think this is a mild addition. Could report UNCERTAIN ADDITION. Actually rule: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" The evidence shows the achievement is for killing Linaniil — \"这个发现\" (this discovery) is arguably incompatible... but the exclamation could refer to anything. I lean UNCERTAIN or empty. Hmm. I'll report UNCERTAIN with ADDITION: target adds \"发现\" which is not in source; the source is a general exclamation. Actually is it worth reporting? It's a name; adding \"发现\" changes meaning somewhat. I'll include UNCERTAIN.\n\nHmm, but caution against over-reporting. The exclamation \"Now, this is impressive!\" in context of killing — the target invents a discovery. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: source: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" target: \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — \"power\" (力量) is omitted; \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" = 对力量与永生的狂热梦想. Target: \"成就你的野心\" (achieved your ambition) — \"power\" dropped, \"wild\" dropped. OMISSION of \"power\". Is it substantive? \"dreams of power and eternal life\" → 野心 covers dreams generally but loses \"power\". Also \"eternal life\" kept. Hmm — \"野心\" (ambition) loosely covers \"power and eternal life\" dreams? It only explicitly mentions eternal life. Omission of \"力量\". Report FINDING OMISSION? It's a partial omission; the meaning \"wild dreams of power\" is fairly significant for a Lichform achievement. I'd report FINDING OMISSION with evidence \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" and correction \"实现了你对力量与永生的狂想：你成为了巫妖！\". Or UNCERTAIN. \"野心\" does encompass desire for power arguably... but combined with only 永恒的生命 mentioned. I'll do FINDING? Hmm. Let me think: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — the target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\" reads as: achieved your ambition AND obtained eternal life. Actually that covers both power (ambition) and eternal life. \"野心\" ≈ ambition for power. It's a reasonable compression. I'd say no objective defect... but \"wild\" omitted, minor. I'll leave empty. Hmm, borderline. I'll leave empty candidates for Q037.\n\nQ038: source: \"Kickin' it old-school\" target: \"现代风格\" — completely opposite! \"old-school\" = 老派/复古; target says 现代风格 (modern style). FINDING, DIRECTION or VALUE. Evidence: \"Kickin' it old-school\". Correction: \"老派风格\" / \"怀旧复古\". Claim_type: DIRECTION (opposite meaning) or OTHER. Use DIRECTION? It's more VALUE (wrong style). I'll use OTHER or DIRECTION. \"old-school\" → modern is an antonym flip: DIRECTION.\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" — matches: the player (main) is dead and kills a boss (BOSS_REVENGE \"Take you with me\"). Fine. p.dead means the main party member is dead. Target fine.\n\nQ040: source: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" target: \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"maintain it in orbit\" = 维持其轨道运行; target says \"稳定在地面上\" (stabilize on the ground) — opposite/orbit omitted. Also \"Abashed Expanse\" translated as 次元浮岛 (a known translation? The zone is a floating shard). The key defect: \"in orbit\" → \"在地面上\". FINDING. Evidence: \"maintain it in orbit\". target_span: \"使其稳定在地面上\". Correction: \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\". Claim_type: VALUE or STATE. Use STATE? \"in orbit\" vs \"on the ground\" — VALUE/STATE. I'll use STATE.\n\nNow double-check Q022 for any issue: source \"The staff will allow us\" — context has \"has allowed\" for one branch; but source given is \"will allow\", target matches. Also \"You cannot stop us now!\" target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — good. Context's alternate has \"It is already too late...\" — not relevant. No findings for Q022.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ028: fine. Actually \"unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" — restless = 烦躁不安/躁动; 蠢蠢欲动 means about to move/start action — acceptable.\n\nQ030: confirm — the menu item is an action on another user in chat, \"Report for bad behavior\" — report that user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" says report my own bad behavior — wrong. FINDING.\n\nQ031: FINDING.\n\nQ034: FINDING.\n\nQ035: FINDING.\n\nQ038: FINDING.\n\nQ040: FINDING.\n\nQ021: FINDING.\n\nQ029: FINDING.\n\nQ032: FINDING.\n\nQ027: UNCERTAIN for \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\". Let me finalize. Also check \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" — \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads fine as future in Chinese (\"到时候肯定准备好了\"). OK.\n\nQ023: I'll include the UNCERTAIN REFERENT for \"凝视着他\". Hmm, actually reconsider: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" — peer out = 向外窥视. Target \"凝视着他\" — the \"他\" refers presumably to the player, but the next line addresses the player as \"你\". Within the same text, \"他\" would be confusing. But is this a \"客观、实质性\" defect? The peering direction and object are added. I'll include UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Evidence: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\". target_span: \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\"。\n\nActually wait — the player is @playerdescriptor.race@, being addressed. The eyes peer out at the player. Using 他 vs 你 — in Chinese game translations, third person for the player is odd but occurs. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ036: UNCERTAIN ADDITION: \"这个发现\" — the source is just an exclamation; the achievement (per context) is for killing Linaniil, not a discovery. I'll make it FINDING? Evidence: \"name = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"LINANIIL_DEAD\\\"\" and desc \"Killed Linaniil\" — but evidence field must be verbatim from source or source_context. I could use \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\" as evidence showing it's a kill not a discovery. Hmm, but the translation is of the name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — the name itself doesn't mention discovery. Adding \"这个发现\" specifies a referent that conflicts with the kill context. I'd say UNCERTAIN is safer. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\". Correction: \"这可真令人印象深刻！\". Verdict UNCERTAIN, claim ADDITION.\n\nHmm, actually reconsider whether to report Q036 at all. \"Now, this is impressive!\" as an achievement name for killing the Supreme Archmage — \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻\" — \"发现\" is a genuine addition not supported. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ027 finalize: UNCERTAIN, claim SUBJECT or OTHER. \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Changes \"our portal attempt\" (our attempt at the portal) to \"when you pass through the portal\". Whose action changed: our → your passing. I'd claim SUBJECT. target_span \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". evidence \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\". Correction: \"这能大大提高你在我们尝试开启传送门时的存活几率。\" Verdict: UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: decide. \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\". \"power\" — 野心 implies ambition which in context = power? Not explicit. \"wild\" omitted. Hmm. Two components: power + eternal life. Target: 野心 (ambition — could cover power) + 永恒的生命. I think this is a defensible compression; not an objective defect. Empty.\n\nActually wait, one more consideration for Q021: the target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" — could the translator have intended a different meaning from source? Source: \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand:\" — the translation flips it to \"even if you know this language, you cannot understand it\". Given source_context, the untranslated text is shown when the player does NOT speak shertul — so \"you do not understand\" is correct; target's version is a different claim. This is an objective change. FINDING, claim CONDITION (negation of condition). target_span \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". evidence \"which you do not understand\". Correction: \"下面是一些你看不懂的文字：\" — well the target only needs correcting the clause: \"你看不懂：\". Correction: \"你看不懂这种语言：\". I'll write correction as \"你看不懂：\" plus keep rest.\n\nNow output JSON with 20 items Q021–Q040 in order, each with observation. Observations in Chinese, brief.\n\nSchema minItems 20 maxItems 20 — exactly 20.\n\nWrite candidates arrays:\n\nQ021: [{FINDING, CONDITION, \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\", \"你看不懂这种语言：\", \"which you do not understand\"}]\n\nQ022: []\n\nQ023: [{UNCERTAIN, REFERENT, \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\", \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\", \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}]\n\nQ024: []\n\nQ025: []\n\nQ026: []\n\nQ027: [{UNCERTAIN, SUBJECT, \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\", \"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\", \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}]\n\nQ028: []\n\nQ029: [{FINDING, STATE, \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\", \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\", \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}]\n\nQ030: [{FINDING, SUBJECT, \"举报我的不良行为\", \"举报不良行为\", \"Report for bad behavior\"}]\n\nQ031: [{FINDING, ACTION, \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\", \"将物品放置到哪里？\", \"Place the object where?\"}]\n\nQ032: [{FINDING, ADDITION, \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\", \"积累3000金币。\", \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}] — hmm, target_span must appear verbatim in target: target is \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — target_span \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\" — appears (without the final 。). Yes. Evidence verbatim from source_context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` — yes appears. But maybe better evidence: the desc for Dragon's Greed is 8000. The finding: the 3000 desc is attached to wrong achievement name. Evidence could be \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" plus id DRAGON_GREED. I'll use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — shows 3000 desc belongs to Treasure Hoarder (its desc is the SOURCE_MATCH). Actually the SOURCE_MATCH_1 is in the Treasure Hoarder block: desc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]], with can_gain who.money >= 3000. So evidence \"return who.money >= 3000\" also good. Use both? Only one evidence string allowed. I'll use `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",`. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim ADDITION.\n\nQ033: []\n\nQ034: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"我一定会让你失望的！\", \"我不会让你失望的！\", \"I will not let you down!\"}]\n\nQ035: [{FINDING, VALUE, \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\", \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\", \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}]\n\nQ036: [{UNCERTAIN, ADDITION, \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"这可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}]\n\nQ037: []\n\nQ038: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"现代风格\", \"老派风格\", \"Kickin' it old-school\"}]\n\nQ039: []\n\nQ040: [{FINDING, STATE, \"使其稳定在地面上\", \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\", \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}]\n\nObservations: brief Chinese descriptions. For empty candidates, observation like \"译文与原文语义一致，未发现可报告的客观缺陷。\"\n\nCheck Q040 claim type: \"in orbit\" vs \"在地面上\" — that's a location/state error; STATE fine.\n\nQ029 STATE fine, or VALUE. Keep STATE.\n\nQ038 DIRECTION (opposite). fine.\n\nQ021 CONDITION fine.\n\nWrite the JSON now. Must be pure JSON, no markdown.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"items\":[{\"neutral_id\":\"Q021\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"CONDITION\",\"target_span\":\"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\",\"correction\":\"你看不懂这种语言：\",\"evidence\":\"which you do not understand\"}],\"observation\":\"原文陈述'你看不懂下面的文字'，译文改为'即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解'，否定了原文条件含义；source_context 显示该未翻译文本仅在玩家不懂 Sher'Tul 语时显示，进一步支持原义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q022\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文与原文语义一致，'will allow' 对应'将让我们得以'，'You cannot stop us now' 对应'你现在已经无法阻止我们了'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q023\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"REFERENT\",\"target_span\":\"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\",\"correction\":\"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\",\"evidence\":\"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}],\"observation\":\"原文'peer out'只表示向外窥视，未指明对象；译文增加'凝视着他'，且下文以'你'称呼对话者，'他'的指代与可见证据的关系存在歧义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q024\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文准确对应原文'你还好么'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q025\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'没能找到所有的指令水晶球'与 'have not been able to find all of the orbs of command' 语义一致，请求部分亦对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q026\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'制作的物品数量'为 'Number of items to make' 的准确对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q027\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"你通过传送门时存活的几率\",\"correction\":\"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\",\"evidence\":\"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}],\"observation\":\"原文说'我们（our）的传送门尝试'，译文改为'你通过传送门时'，动作主体与场景有所偏移，但'portal attempt'本身略有歧义，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q028\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'你效力的时候到了'对应 'you are called to serve'，其余部分对应良好；'这一切的源头'为与证据相容的少量补充，不构成缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q029\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\",\"correction\":\"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\",\"evidence\":\"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Nothing but hatchlings' 意为'到目前为止只有幼龙'，译文'从未遇上幼龙'含义相反，且与后文'龙皮不够'的逻辑矛盾。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q030\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"举报我的不良行为\",\"correction\":\"举报不良行为\",\"evidence\":\"Report for bad behavior\"}],\"observation\":\"这是对其他用户操作的菜单项，原文无'我的'；译文加入'我的'后变成举报自己的不良行为，主体指向错误。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q031\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ACTION\",\"target_span\":\"将物品丢弃到哪里？\",\"correction\":\"将物品放置到哪里？\",\"evidence\":\"Place the object where?\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Place' 为中性'放置'，source_context 显示选项包含放入背包与丢弃两种；译文'丢弃'把动作窄化为丢弃之一，与选项集合不符。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q032\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\",\"correction\":\"积累3000金币。\",\"evidence\":\"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}],\"observation\":\"原文仅为'Amassed 3000 gold pieces.'；译文附加'在“龙之贪婪”成就中'，而 source_context 显示该描述属于 'Treasure Hoarder'（3000金币），Dragon's Greed 的描述为8000金币，新增信息与可见证据冲突。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q033\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰'与原文一致，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q034\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"我一定会让你失望的！\",\"correction\":\"我不会让你失望的！\",\"evidence\":\"I will not let you down!\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'I will not let you down' 为否定（不会让你失望），译文'我一定会让你失望的'含义完全相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q035\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"VALUE\",\"target_span\":\"竞技场生存至第20轮。\",\"correction\":\"竞技场生存至第50轮。\",\"evidence\":\"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为第50波，译文写为第20轮，数值错误；source_context 中第20波属于另一成就 'Arena Battler 20'。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q036\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"correction\":\"这可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"evidence\":\"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为泛指的感叹'Now, this is impressive!'，译文添加'这个发现'；结合 source_context 该成就对应击杀事件而非发现，新增指涉与证据存在张力，但成就名可作宽松修辞，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q037\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命'可视为对 'wild dreams of power and eternal life' 的压缩表达，力量含义由'野心'承载，未构成可客观判定的实质性缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q038\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"现代风格\",\"correction\":\"老派风格\",\"evidence\":\"Kickin' it old-school\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'old-school' 意为老派、复古，译文'现代风格'含义相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q039\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS'与 'Killed a boss while already dead' 语义一致，source_context 中 can_gain 判定亦相符，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q040\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"使其稳定在地面上\",\"correction\":\"使其稳定维持在轨道上\",\"evidence\":\"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为'maintain it in orbit'（维持其轨道运行），译文'稳定在地面上'与轨道状态相悖。\"}]}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai-standard-cn","model":"glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":8920,"output":7825,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6270,"totalTokens":16745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787984354413,"responseId":"202608291419144ae2b1e046524199","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze each item.\n\nQ021: source: \"which you do not understand: #{italic}#...\" target: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：...\" Source says \"which you do not understand\" — target says \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" (\"even if you know this language, you cannot understand\"). That's a negation flip. Source: you do not understand. Target: even if you know this language, you cannot understand. Hmm, source_context: the lore branch when player does NOT speak shertul shows \"which you do not understand:\" followed by the untranslated text; when speaks_shertul, shows translation. The source string is the \"which you do not understand\" variant. Target adds \"即使你懂得这种语言\" — actually this inverts: source states player doesn't understand; target says even if you know the language you cannot understand. This is a negation/condition defect. FINDING, CONDITION or STATE. Evidence: \"which you do not understand\". target_span: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". Correction: \"你看不懂：\" or similar. Actually source says \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand\" — the text underneath which you do not understand. Correction: \"下面有一些你看不懂的文字：\". FINDING, CONDITION (negation flipped). Claim_type: CONDITION or STATE. Use CONDITION.\n\nWait—but the source_context shows the two branches: untranslated text shown when player does NOT speak shertul, translated when does. The target's \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" contradicts: source's branch shows the untranslated string precisely because you don't understand. Actually target says even if you know the language you can't understand it — the string \"Sho ch'zun...\" is shertul language, untranslated. In source, \"which you do not understand\" is the correct meaning. Target changes to \"even if you understand this language, you cannot understand\" — flip. FINDING.\n\nQ022: source: \"The staff will allow us to drain...\" target: \"这根法杖将让我们得以...\" OK. Source context has \"The staff has allowed us\" but the source given says \"will allow\". Translation matches source \"will allow\" — 将让我们得以. Fine. Also last line: \"You cannot stop us now!\" → \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — \"You cannot stop us now\" means \"你们现在无法阻止我们\" (you are unable to stop us). Target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了\" — same meaning. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ023: source: \"What do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\" target: \"你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\" Fine. The italic part: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" → \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\" — \"peer out\" = 向外窥视/望出来. Target says \"凝视着他\" — at him? Source doesn't specify object. \"peer out\" — looking out through the slot. \"凝视着他\" adds \"him\" — could be the NPC peering out at the player. Minor addition but compatible with context (the NPC peers out at the player who's at the door). \"gaze at him\" — the player is the one addressed; the eyes peer out at... the player. But target uses \"他\" (him) while the addressee is the player (\"你\"). Also \"A slot in the door opens\" → \"门上开了一个小洞\" — slot = 狭缝/小口, \"小洞\" is a hole, minor. \"凝视着他\" vs \"向外窥视\" — the pronoun 他 refers to whom? If the eyes belong to the doorkeeper, they peer out at the player, so should be \"你\" or just \"向外张望\". Is this an objective defect? The \"him\" as referent is wrong-ish—the addressee is the player addressed as \"你\". But it could refer to a third person present. Hmm. It's a mild referent issue. I'd report as UNCERTAIN maybe. Actually rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence isn't a defect. The peering is at whoever is at the door; in the dialog the player. Using 他 while addressing 你 is inconsistent but possibly a translation convention. I'll report UNCERTAIN for REFERENT? Or skip. Also \"peer out\" means to look out from within; \"凝视着他\" adds a direction. I think it's low severity; I might report UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Hmm, let me be careful about false positives. The main sentence is fine. I'll leave candidates empty for Q023? The \"他\" is the most questionable. The dialog is between NPC and player; eyes peer out and look at the player (\"你\"). Translating as \"他\" introduces third-person referent not in source. I'd report as FINDING? It's fairly subjective. I'll do UNCERTAIN with REFERENT.\n\nQ024: \"Aeryn, are you well?\" → \"艾琳，你还好么？\" Fine. No defect.\n\nQ025: source: \"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\" target: \"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\" Fine. \"orbs of command\" → 指令水晶球 — okay, orb = 球. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ026: \"Number of items to make\" → \"制作的物品数量\" Fine.\n\nQ027: source: \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" target: \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Hmm \"and I'll have everything prepared\" — future: \"我就会把一切都准备好\". Target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" adds certainty, and \"准备好了\" perfective. Minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" = 届时我会把一切都准备好. Target is close. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will surely have everything ready\" — acceptable. Second: \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago.\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。\" Fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\" — \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\" — our attempt to create the portal / portal attempt. Target says \"你通过传送门时\" (when you pass through the portal). Source: \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt at the portal (creating/opening portal). Hmm — \"surviving our portal attempt\" — could be surviving the attempt to open the portal. Target shifts to surviving passing through the portal. Is that a defect? \"our portal attempt\" is ambiguous; the risk is during the portal creation/travel. The target changes \"our\" to \"你\" and \"attempt\" to \"通过传送门时\". This changes subject: our attempt → your passing through. I'd report as FINDING? It's arguably ambiguous. \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt involving the portal they will create for the player. \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\" = your odds of surviving when you go through the portal. Source: your odds of surviving our attempt at the portal. These differ: whose action. \"our\" vs \"your\". I'd report FINDING with SUBJECT/OTHER? Or UNCERTAIN. Hmm. The safest: report UNCERTAIN with claim OTHER or SUBJECT. Evidence: \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\". target_span: \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Correction: \"我们尝试开启传送门时你存活的几率\" or \"你在我们尝试传送时存活的几率\". I'll mark FINDING? The change of \"our\" to \"你\" is objective. But \"portal attempt\" could mean \"attempt to use the portal\" — still \"our attempt\". The target removes \"our\". I'll do UNCERTAIN.\n\nActually also \"Return in a few days\" — 几天后你回来 fine.\n\nQ028: source: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" fine. \"The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\" fine. \"You must go there and find the source.\" → \"你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\" \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — minor addition, compatible. Fine.\n\nQ029: source: \"Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain\" → \"探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽\" fine. \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" Hmm — \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" means: so far we've only encountered hatchlings (nothing but = only). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings — that's the OPPOSITE! Source: only hatchlings (no adult dragons). Target: never met hatchlings. That's a clear negation flip / value error. FINDING. Evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" target_span: \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\"。 Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到过幼龙\". Claim_type: OTHER or VALUE/STATE. Use STATE? It's about what they've encountered. I'd use VALUE or STATE. Let's use STATE.\n\nWait — could \"Nothing but hatchlings\" mean \"nothing except hatchlings\" i.e., only hatchlings so far — yes. And the rest: \"if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon\" — consistent with only finding hatchlings (not enough dragonhide). Target \"从未遇上幼龙\" contradicts. Definitely FINDING.\n\nAlso \"Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know\" → \"高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人\" — \"money-grubbing\" included as 贪财, Thronesmen → 钢铁王座 (Throne). Fine. \"Xann\" → 希安. \"wyrmic\" → 龙战士 — wyrmic is a class; 龙战士 acceptable. \"if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\" → \"现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\" — \"draconic talents\" → 操控龙族力量的本事 — addition but compatible. Fine.\n\nSo Q029 has one FINDING.\n\nQ030: source: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — \"my\" is added; source is a menu action to report a user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" = report MY bad behavior — wrong direction! It should be \"举报不良行为\" (report [them] for bad behavior). Adding \"我的\" reverses the meaning. FINDING. Evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\". target_span \"举报我的不良行为\". Correction: \"举报不良行为\". Claim_type: SUBJECT or DIRECTION. Use SUBJECT? Or ADDITION. I'd say SUBJECT (who did bad behavior). Or DIRECTION. I'll use SUBJECT.\n\nQ031: source: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" ≠ \"丢弃\" (drop). The popup offers both inventory and drop options, so \"放置\" is correct; \"丢弃\" narrows to drop. FINDING. Evidence: \"Place the object where?\" target_span \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\". Claim_type: ACTION. Note source_context shows options include \"Inventory of %s\" and \"Drop @\" — supporting that place ≠ only drop. That context supports the finding.\n\nQ032: source: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" target: \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" — target adds \"在'龙之贪婪'成就中\". From source_context, the achievement with 3000 is \"Treasure Hoarder\"; Dragon's Greed is 8000. So the addition is wrong info — it attaches the desc to Dragon's Greed achievement, but 3000 corresponds to Treasure Hoarder. However, the rule: addition compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong by evidence? The context shows DRAGON_GREED desc = 8000. So adding \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" to a 3000 desc is contradicted by visible evidence. FINDING. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" for DRAGON_GREED, and the 3000 desc belongs to \"Treasure Hoarder\". Evidence must be verbatim from source_context: I can quote \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" and \"return who.money >= 3000\". Evidence string should be verbatim occurrence. I'll use: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" ... hmm evidence must be a single verbatim string. Use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — verbatim in context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` yes. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim_type: ADDITION.\n\nQ033: \"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\" → \"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\" Fine. Note in context this is \"Almost Master of Arena\" but translation only handles desc; fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite! \"let you down\" = 让你失望; \"I will NOT let you down\" = 我不会让你失望. Target says \"我一定会让你失望的\" = I will definitely disappoint you. FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"I will not let you down!\" Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\".\n\nQ035: source: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" target: \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20. FINDING, VALUE. Evidence: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" Correction: \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\"\n\nQ036: source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" target: \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" but compatible-ish. Source is an achievement name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — actually from context it's an achievement name for killing Linaniil. Adding \"发现\" — hmm, is that judgeable wrong? Source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" — \"这可真令人印象深刻！\" Target adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). The achievement is about a kill, not a discovery. But by visible evidence alone, \"this discovery\" is an addition that specifies the referent as a discovery. Is it \"compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong\"? The context desc: \"Killed Linaniil...\" — killing isn't a discovery. Hmm, achievements can be named loosely. I think this is a mild addition. Could report UNCERTAIN ADDITION. Actually rule: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" The evidence shows the achievement is for killing Linaniil — \"这个发现\" (this discovery) is arguably incompatible... but the exclamation could refer to anything. I lean UNCERTAIN or empty. Hmm. I'll report UNCERTAIN with ADDITION: target adds \"发现\" which is not in source; the source is a general exclamation. Actually is it worth reporting? It's a name; adding \"发现\" changes meaning somewhat. I'll include UNCERTAIN.\n\nHmm, but caution against over-reporting. The exclamation \"Now, this is impressive!\" in context of killing — the target invents a discovery. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: source: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" target: \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — \"power\" (力量) is omitted; \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" = 对力量与永生的狂热梦想. Target: \"成就你的野心\" (achieved your ambition) — \"power\" dropped, \"wild\" dropped. OMISSION of \"power\". Is it substantive? \"dreams of power and eternal life\" → 野心 covers dreams generally but loses \"power\". Also \"eternal life\" kept. Hmm — \"野心\" (ambition) loosely covers \"power and eternal life\" dreams? It only explicitly mentions eternal life. Omission of \"力量\". Report FINDING OMISSION? It's a partial omission; the meaning \"wild dreams of power\" is fairly significant for a Lichform achievement. I'd report FINDING OMISSION with evidence \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" and correction \"实现了你对力量与永生的狂想：你成为了巫妖！\". Or UNCERTAIN. \"野心\" does encompass desire for power arguably... but combined with only 永恒的生命 mentioned. I'll do FINDING? Hmm. Let me think: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — the target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\" reads as: achieved your ambition AND obtained eternal life. Actually that covers both power (ambition) and eternal life. \"野心\" ≈ ambition for power. It's a reasonable compression. I'd say no objective defect... but \"wild\" omitted, minor. I'll leave empty. Hmm, borderline. I'll leave empty candidates for Q037.\n\nQ038: source: \"Kickin' it old-school\" target: \"现代风格\" — completely opposite! \"old-school\" = 老派/复古; target says 现代风格 (modern style). FINDING, DIRECTION or VALUE. Evidence: \"Kickin' it old-school\". Correction: \"老派风格\" / \"怀旧复古\". Claim_type: DIRECTION (opposite meaning) or OTHER. Use DIRECTION? It's more VALUE (wrong style). I'll use OTHER or DIRECTION. \"old-school\" → modern is an antonym flip: DIRECTION.\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" — matches: the player (main) is dead and kills a boss (BOSS_REVENGE \"Take you with me\"). Fine. p.dead means the main party member is dead. Target fine.\n\nQ040: source: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" target: \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"maintain it in orbit\" = 维持其轨道运行; target says \"稳定在地面上\" (stabilize on the ground) — opposite/orbit omitted. Also \"Abashed Expanse\" translated as 次元浮岛 (a known translation? The zone is a floating shard). The key defect: \"in orbit\" → \"在地面上\". FINDING. Evidence: \"maintain it in orbit\". target_span: \"使其稳定在地面上\". Correction: \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\". Claim_type: VALUE or STATE. Use STATE? \"in orbit\" vs \"on the ground\" — VALUE/STATE. I'll use STATE.\n\nNow double-check Q022 for any issue: source \"The staff will allow us\" — context has \"has allowed\" for one branch; but source given is \"will allow\", target matches. Also \"You cannot stop us now!\" target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — good. Context's alternate has \"It is already too late...\" — not relevant. No findings for Q022.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ028: fine. Actually \"unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" — restless = 烦躁不安/躁动; 蠢蠢欲动 means about to move/start action — acceptable.\n\nQ030: confirm — the menu item is an action on another user in chat, \"Report for bad behavior\" — report that user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" says report my own bad behavior — wrong. FINDING.\n\nQ031: FINDING.\n\nQ034: FINDING.\n\nQ035: FINDING.\n\nQ038: FINDING.\n\nQ040: FINDING.\n\nQ021: FINDING.\n\nQ029: FINDING.\n\nQ032: FINDING.\n\nQ027: UNCERTAIN for \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\". Let me finalize. Also check \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" — \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads fine as future in Chinese (\"到时候肯定准备好了\"). OK.\n\nQ023: I'll include the UNCERTAIN REFERENT for \"凝视着他\". Hmm, actually reconsider: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" — peer out = 向外窥视. Target \"凝视着他\" — the \"他\" refers presumably to the player, but the next line addresses the player as \"你\". Within the same text, \"他\" would be confusing. But is this a \"客观、实质性\" defect? The peering direction and object are added. I'll include UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Evidence: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\". target_span: \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\"。\n\nActually wait — the player is @playerdescriptor.race@, being addressed. The eyes peer out at the player. Using 他 vs 你 — in Chinese game translations, third person for the player is odd but occurs. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ036: UNCERTAIN ADDITION: \"这个发现\" — the source is just an exclamation; the achievement (per context) is for killing Linaniil, not a discovery. I'll make it FINDING? Evidence: \"name = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"LINANIIL_DEAD\\\"\" and desc \"Killed Linaniil\" — but evidence field must be verbatim from source or source_context. I could use \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\" as evidence showing it's a kill not a discovery. Hmm, but the translation is of the name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — the name itself doesn't mention discovery. Adding \"这个发现\" specifies a referent that conflicts with the kill context. I'd say UNCERTAIN is safer. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\". Correction: \"这可真令人印象深刻！\". Verdict UNCERTAIN, claim ADDITION.\n\nHmm, actually reconsider whether to report Q036 at all. \"Now, this is impressive!\" as an achievement name for killing the Supreme Archmage — \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻\" — \"发现\" is a genuine addition not supported. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ027 finalize: UNCERTAIN, claim SUBJECT or OTHER. \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Changes \"our portal attempt\" (our attempt at the portal) to \"when you pass through the portal\". Whose action changed: our → your passing. I'd claim SUBJECT. target_span \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". evidence \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\". Correction: \"这能大大提高你在我们尝试开启传送门时的存活几率。\" Verdict: UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: decide. \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\". \"power\" — 野心 implies ambition which in context = power? Not explicit. \"wild\" omitted. Hmm. Two components: power + eternal life. Target: 野心 (ambition — could cover power) + 永恒的生命. I think this is a defensible compression; not an objective defect. Empty.\n\nActually wait, one more consideration for Q021: the target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" — could the translator have intended a different meaning from source? Source: \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand:\" — the translation flips it to \"even if you know this language, you cannot understand it\". Given source_context, the untranslated text is shown when the player does NOT speak shertul — so \"you do not understand\" is correct; target's version is a different claim. This is an objective change. FINDING, claim CONDITION (negation of condition). target_span \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". evidence \"which you do not understand\". Correction: \"下面是一些你看不懂的文字：\" — well the target only needs correcting the clause: \"你看不懂：\". Correction: \"你看不懂这种语言：\". I'll write correction as \"你看不懂：\" plus keep rest.\n\nNow output JSON with 20 items Q021–Q040 in order, each with observation. Observations in Chinese, brief.\n\nSchema minItems 20 maxItems 20 — exactly 20.\n\nWrite candidates arrays:\n\nQ021: [{FINDING, CONDITION, \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\", \"你看不懂这种语言：\", \"which you do not understand\"}]\n\nQ022: []\n\nQ023: [{UNCERTAIN, REFERENT, \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\", \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\", \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}]\n\nQ024: []\n\nQ025: []\n\nQ026: []\n\nQ027: [{UNCERTAIN, SUBJECT, \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\", \"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\", \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}]\n\nQ028: []\n\nQ029: [{FINDING, STATE, \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\", \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\", \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}]\n\nQ030: [{FINDING, SUBJECT, \"举报我的不良行为\", \"举报不良行为\", \"Report for bad behavior\"}]\n\nQ031: [{FINDING, ACTION, \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\", \"将物品放置到哪里？\", \"Place the object where?\"}]\n\nQ032: [{FINDING, ADDITION, \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\", \"积累3000金币。\", \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}] — hmm, target_span must appear verbatim in target: target is \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — target_span \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\" — appears (without the final 。). Yes. Evidence verbatim from source_context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` — yes appears. But maybe better evidence: the desc for Dragon's Greed is 8000. The finding: the 3000 desc is attached to wrong achievement name. Evidence could be \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" plus id DRAGON_GREED. I'll use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — shows 3000 desc belongs to Treasure Hoarder (its desc is the SOURCE_MATCH). Actually the SOURCE_MATCH_1 is in the Treasure Hoarder block: desc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]], with can_gain who.money >= 3000. So evidence \"return who.money >= 3000\" also good. Use both? Only one evidence string allowed. I'll use `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",`. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim ADDITION.\n\nQ033: []\n\nQ034: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"我一定会让你失望的！\", \"我不会让你失望的！\", \"I will not let you down!\"}]\n\nQ035: [{FINDING, VALUE, \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\", \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\", \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}]\n\nQ036: [{UNCERTAIN, ADDITION, \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"这可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}]\n\nQ037: []\n\nQ038: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"现代风格\", \"老派风格\", \"Kickin' it old-school\"}]\n\nQ039: []\n\nQ040: [{FINDING, STATE, \"使其稳定在地面上\", \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\", \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}]\n\nObservations: brief Chinese descriptions. For empty candidates, observation like \"译文与原文语义一致，未发现可报告的客观缺陷。\"\n\nCheck Q040 claim type: \"in orbit\" vs \"在地面上\" — that's a location/state error; STATE fine.\n\nQ029 STATE fine, or VALUE. Keep STATE.\n\nQ038 DIRECTION (opposite). fine.\n\nQ021 CONDITION fine.\n\nWrite the JSON now. Must be pure JSON, no markdown.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"items\":[{\"neutral_id\":\"Q021\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"CONDITION\",\"target_span\":\"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\",\"correction\":\"你看不懂这种语言：\",\"evidence\":\"which you do not understand\"}],\"observation\":\"原文陈述'你看不懂下面的文字'，译文改为'即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解'，否定了原文条件含义；source_context 显示该未翻译文本仅在玩家不懂 Sher'Tul 语时显示，进一步支持原义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q022\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文与原文语义一致，'will allow' 对应'将让我们得以'，'You cannot stop us now' 对应'你现在已经无法阻止我们了'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q023\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"REFERENT\",\"target_span\":\"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\",\"correction\":\"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\",\"evidence\":\"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}],\"observation\":\"原文'peer out'只表示向外窥视，未指明对象；译文增加'凝视着他'，且下文以'你'称呼对话者，'他'的指代与可见证据的关系存在歧义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q024\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文准确对应原文'你还好么'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q025\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'没能找到所有的指令水晶球'与 'have not been able to find all of the orbs of command' 语义一致，请求部分亦对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q026\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'制作的物品数量'为 'Number of items to make' 的准确对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q027\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"你通过传送门时存活的几率\",\"correction\":\"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\",\"evidence\":\"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}],\"observation\":\"原文说'我们（our）的传送门尝试'，译文改为'你通过传送门时'，动作主体与场景有所偏移，但'portal attempt'本身略有歧义，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q028\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'你效力的时候到了'对应 'you are called to serve'，其余部分对应良好；'这一切的源头'为与证据相容的少量补充，不构成缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q029\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\",\"correction\":\"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\",\"evidence\":\"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Nothing but hatchlings' 意为'到目前为止只有幼龙'，译文'从未遇上幼龙'含义相反，且与后文'龙皮不够'的逻辑矛盾。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q030\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"举报我的不良行为\",\"correction\":\"举报不良行为\",\"evidence\":\"Report for bad behavior\"}],\"observation\":\"这是对其他用户操作的菜单项，原文无'我的'；译文加入'我的'后变成举报自己的不良行为，主体指向错误。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q031\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ACTION\",\"target_span\":\"将物品丢弃到哪里？\",\"correction\":\"将物品放置到哪里？\",\"evidence\":\"Place the object where?\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Place' 为中性'放置'，source_context 显示选项包含放入背包与丢弃两种；译文'丢弃'把动作窄化为丢弃之一，与选项集合不符。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q032\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\",\"correction\":\"积累3000金币。\",\"evidence\":\"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}],\"observation\":\"原文仅为'Amassed 3000 gold pieces.'；译文附加'在“龙之贪婪”成就中'，而 source_context 显示该描述属于 'Treasure Hoarder'（3000金币），Dragon's Greed 的描述为8000金币，新增信息与可见证据冲突。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q033\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰'与原文一致，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q034\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"我一定会让你失望的！\",\"correction\":\"我不会让你失望的！\",\"evidence\":\"I will not let you down!\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'I will not let you down' 为否定（不会让你失望），译文'我一定会让你失望的'含义完全相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q035\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"VALUE\",\"target_span\":\"竞技场生存至第20轮。\",\"correction\":\"竞技场生存至第50轮。\",\"evidence\":\"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为第50波，译文写为第20轮，数值错误；source_context 中第20波属于另一成就 'Arena Battler 20'。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q036\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"correction\":\"这可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"evidence\":\"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为泛指的感叹'Now, this is impressive!'，译文添加'这个发现'；结合 source_context 该成就对应击杀事件而非发现，新增指涉与证据存在张力，但成就名可作宽松修辞，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q037\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命'可视为对 'wild dreams of power and eternal life' 的压缩表达，力量含义由'野心'承载，未构成可客观判定的实质性缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q038\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"现代风格\",\"correction\":\"老派风格\",\"evidence\":\"Kickin' it old-school\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'old-school' 意为老派、复古，译文'现代风格'含义相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q039\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS'与 'Killed a boss while already dead' 语义一致，source_context 中 can_gain 判定亦相符，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q040\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"使其稳定在地面上\",\"correction\":\"使其稳定维持在轨道上\",\"evidence\":\"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为'maintain it in orbit'（维持其轨道运行），译文'稳定在地面上'与轨道状态相悖。\"}]}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai-standard-cn","model":"glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":8920,"output":7825,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6270,"totalTokens":16745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787984354413,"responseId":"202608291419144ae2b1e046524199","rawStopReason":"stop"},"toolResults":[]}
{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是双语翻译审核员。逐条比较英文 source 与中文 target，判断是否存在客观、实质性的翻译缺陷。\n\n规则：\n\n1. 只报告可由本请求中可见文本直接支持的客观问题；不要依赖外部知识、仓库记忆、猜测或风格偏好。\n2. 若条目包含 source_context，可把它作为与 source 同等有效的源码证据；若没有，则只能使用 source 与 target。\n3. 新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\n4. FINDING 表示证据足以确定存在缺陷；UNCERTAIN 仅用于证据指向问题但仍有真实歧义；没有可报告的客观问题时 candidates 为空数组。\n5. 一个条目可报告多个相互独立的候选。不要因为发现一个问题而停止检查，也不要让错误候选抵消正确候选。\n6. 每个候选的 target_span 必须逐字出现在 target 中；evidence 必须逐字出现在 source，或在该条目存在时逐字出现在 source_context 中。\n7. 保持输入顺序和 neutral_id 完全不变。严格输出符合给定 schema 的 JSON，不要输出 Markdown 或额外说明。\n\n缺陷类型：VALUE、DIRECTION、CONDITION、SUBJECT、REFERENT、TIMING、SCOPE、ACTION、STATE、ORDER、OMISSION、ADDITION、OTHER。\n\n输出 JSON Schema（逐字遵守）：\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"items\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 20,\n      \"maxItems\": 20,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"required\": [\"neutral_id\", \"candidates\", \"observation\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"neutral_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^Q[0-9]{3}$\"},\n          \"candidates\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"maxItems\": 4,\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\n              \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"claim_type\", \"target_span\", \"correction\", \"evidence\"],\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"FINDING\", \"UNCERTAIN\"]},\n                \"claim_type\": {\"enum\": [\"VALUE\", \"DIRECTION\", \"CONDITION\", \"SUBJECT\", \"REFERENT\", \"TIMING\", \"SCOPE\", \"ACTION\", \"STATE\", \"ORDER\", \"OMISSION\", \"ADDITION\", \"OTHER\"]},\n                \"target_span\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                \"correction\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"observation\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n输入 JSON：\n{\"schema_version\":\"source-context-controlled-confirmation-request-b-v2\",\"items\":[{\"neutral_id\":\"Q021\",\"source\":\"which you do not understand: #{italic}#'Sho ch'zun Eyal mor donuth, ik ranaheli donoth trun ze.'#{normal}#\",\"target\":\"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：#{italic}#'Sho ch'zun Eyal mor donuth, ik ranaheli donoth trun ze.'#{normal}#\",\"source_context\":\"-- darkgod@te4.org\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n-- Sher'Tul\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nnewLore{\\n\\tid = \\\"shertul-fortress-1\\\",\\n\\tcategory = \\\"sher'tul\\\",\\n\\tname = _t\\\"first mural painting\\\", always_pop = true,\\n\\timage = \\\"shertul_fortress_lore1.png\\\",\\n\\tlore = function() return _t[[You see here a mural showing a dark and tortured world. Large, god-like figures with powerful auras fight each other, and the earth is torn beneath their feet.\\nThere is some text underneath ]]..(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]] or _t[[#{italic}#'In the beginning the world was dark, and the petty gods fought over their broken lands.'#{normal}#]])\\n\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewLore{\\n\\tid = \\\"shertul-fortress-2\\\",\\n\\tcategory = \\\"sher'tul\\\",\\n\\tname = _t\\\"second mural painting\\\", always_pop = true,\\n\\timage = \\\"shertul_fortress_lore2.png\\\",\\n\\tlore = function() return _t[[In this picture a huge god with glowing eyes towers above the land, and in his right hand he holds high the sun. The other gods are running from him, wincing from the light.\\nThere is some text underneath ]]..(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[which you do not understand: #{italic}#'Fa AMAKTHEL tabak, ik koru bazan tro yu, ik ranaheli tobol don schek ruun. Ik blana dem Soli as banafel ik goriz uf Eyal ik blod, \\\"Tro fasa goru domus asam, ik goru domit tro Eyal.\\\"'#{normal}#]] or _t[[#{italic}#'But AMAKTHEL came, and his might surpassed all else, and the petty gods fled before his glory. And he made the Sun from his breath and held it above the world and said, \\\"All that this light touches shall be mine, and this light shall touch all the world.'#{normal}#]])\\n\\tend,\\n}\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q022\",\"source\":\"The Creator. The God who made this world, He who watched silently as the races fought and burnt the land.\\nHe who felt great sorrow for this world. He who shall now shatter the barriers of this world to remake it, only better!\\nThe staff will allow us to drain enough energy from this world to open the portal to the Void and summon Him through!\\nYou cannot stop us now!\",\"target\":\"造物主，创造这个世界的神。他默默注视着各个种族争战不休，将大地付之一炬。\\n他为这个世界深感悲痛。如今他将击碎这个世界的屏障，将它重塑得更加美好！\\n这根法杖将让我们得以从这个世界抽取足够的能量，打开通往虚空的传送门并召唤他降临！\\n你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\",\"source_context\":\"newChat{ id=\\\"explain3\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[The Creator. The God who made this world, He who watched silently as the races fought and burnt the land.\\nHe who felt great sorrow for this world. He who shall now shatter the barriers of this world to remake it, only better!\\nThe staff has allowed us to drain enough energy from this world to open the portal to the Void and summon Him through!\\nIt is already too late. He is coming through as we speak -- it is only a matter of hours!]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I *WILL* stop you! The world will not end today!\\\", jump=\\\"aeryn\\\", switch_npc={name=_t\\\"High Sun Paladin Aeryn\\\", image=\\\"npc/humanoid_human_high_sun_paladin_aeryn.png\\\"}, action=aeryn_comes, cond=aeryn_alive},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I *WILL* stop you! The world will not end today!\\\", cond=aeryn_dead},\\n\\t}\\n}\\nelse\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"explain3\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I *WILL* stop you! The world will not end today!\\\", jump=\\\"aeryn\\\", switch_npc={name=_t\\\"High Sun Paladin Aeryn\\\", image=\\\"npc/humanoid_human_high_sun_paladin_aeryn.png\\\"}, action=aeryn_comes, cond=aeryn_alive},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I *WILL* stop you! The world will not end today!\\\", cond=aeryn_dead},\\n\\t}\\n}\\nend\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"aeryn\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[#LIGHT_GREEN#*The air whirls at your side and suddenly High Sun Paladin Aeryn appears!*#WHITE#\\nThen you shall not fight alone! Together we shall stop them, or die trying!]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I am glad to have you at my side, my Lady. Let's hunt some wizards!\\\"},\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q023\",\"source\":\"#LIGHT_GREEN#*A slot in the door opens and a pair of wild eyes peer out.*#WHITE#\\nWhat do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\",\"target\":\"#LIGHT_GREEN#*门上开了一个小洞，一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他。*#WHITE#\\n你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\",\"source_context\":\"\\nlocal function check_materials(npc, player)\\n\\tlocal gem_o, gem_item, gem_inven_id = player:findInAllInventories(\\\"Resonating Diamond\\\", {raw_name=true})\\n\\tlocal athame_o, athame_item, athame_inven_id = player:findInAllInventories(\\\"Blood-Runed Athame\\\", {raw_name=true})\\n\\treturn gem_o and athame_o and player.money >= 100\\nend\\n\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\n-- Main dialog\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"welcome\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"Paladin Aeryn told me that you could help me. I need to get to Maj'Eyal.\\\", jump=\\\"help\\\", cond=function(npc, player) return game.state:isAdvanced() and not player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\") end},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I found the Blood-Runed Athame, but there was no Resonating Diamond.\\\", jump=\\\"athame\\\", cond=function(npc, player) return player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\") and player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\"):isCompleted(\\\"athame\\\") and not player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\"):isCompleted(\\\"gem\\\") end},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I have a Resonating Diamond.\\\", jump=\\\"complete\\\", cond=function(npc, player) return player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\") and player:hasQuest(\\\"west-portal\\\"):isCompleted(\\\"gem\\\") end},\\n\\t\\t{_t(\\\"Sorry, I have to go!\\\", \\\"chat_zemekkys\\\")},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\n-- Give quest\\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"help\\\",\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q024\",\"source\":\"Aeryn, are you well?\",\"target\":\"艾琳，你还好么？\",\"source_context\":\"\\t\\tend},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\n----------- If the void portal is still closed\\nelse\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"welcome\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[#LIGHT_GREEN#*The two Sorcerers lie dead before you.*#WHITE#\\n#LIGHT_GREEN#*Their bodies vanish in some immaterial mist.*#WHITE#\\nYou have won the game!\\nBoth Maj'Eyal and the Far East are safe from the dark schemes of the Sorcerers and their God.]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", jump=\\\"aeryn-ok\\\", switch_npc=aeryn_alive(), cond=aeryn_alive},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"[leave]\\\", action=function(npc, player) player:hasQuest(\\\"high-peak\\\"):win(\\\"full\\\") end},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"aeryn-ok\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[I cannot believe we succeeded. I was prepared to die and yet I live.\\nI might have underestimated you. You did more than we could have hoped for!]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"We both did.\\\", action=function(npc, player) player:hasQuest(\\\"high-peak\\\"):win(\\\"full\\\") end},\\n\\t}\\n}\\nend\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q025\",\"source\":\"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\",\"target\":\"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\",\"source_context\":\"\\t\\t{_t\\\"Maybe I'll visit him. Thank you.\\\", jump=\\\"welcome\\\"},\\n\\t},\\n}\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"prides-dead\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[The news has indeed reached me. I could scarce believe it, so long have we been at war with the Pride.\\nNow they are dead? At the hands of just one @playerdescriptor.race@? Truly I am amazed by your power.\\nWhile you were busy bringing an end to the orcs, we managed to discover some parts of the truth from a captive orc.\\nHe talked about the shield protecting the High Peak. It seems to be controlled by \\\"orbs of command\\\" which the masters of the Prides had in their possession.\\nHe also said the only way to enter the peak and de-activate the shield is through the \\\"slime tunnels\\\", located somewhere in one of the Prides, probably Grushnak.\\n]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\",\\n\\t\\tjump=\\\"prides-dead-orbs-missing\\\",\\n\\t\\tcond=function(npc, player) return not (game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_DRAGON\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_DESTRUCTION\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_UNDEATH\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_ELEMENTS\\\")) end\\n\\t\\t},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"Thanks, my lady. I will look for the tunnel and venture inside the Peak.\\\", \\n\\t\\tcond=function(npc, player) return (game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_DRAGON\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_DESTRUCTION\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_UNDEATH\\\") and game.party:findInAllPartyInventoriesBy(\\\"define_as\\\", \\\"ORB_ELEMENTS\\\")) end,\\n\\t\\taction=function(npc, player)\\n\\t\\t\\tplayer:setQuestStatus(\\\"orc-pride\\\", engine.Quest.DONE)\\n\\t\\t\\tplayer:grantQuest(\\\"high-peak\\\")\\n\\t\\tend},\\n\\t},\\n}\\n\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q026\",\"source\":\"Number of items to make\",\"target\":\"制作的物品数量\",\"source_context\":\"\\tif not item then return end\\n\\n\\tif item.action then\\n\\t\\titem:action()\\n\\telseif item.unique then\\n\\t\\tlocal n = not item.error and item.obj or game.zone:finishEntity(game.level, \\\"object\\\", item.e)\\n\\t\\tif n then\\n\\t\\t\\tn:identify(true)\\n\\t\\t\\tself:acceptObject(n)\\n\\t\\tend\\n\\telse\\n\\t\\tlocal example = item.obj and not item.error\\n\\t\\tgame:registerDialog(GetQuantity.new(_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", (\\\"Enter 1-100%s\\\"):tformat(example and _t\\\", or 0 for the example item\\\" or \\\"\\\"), 20, 100, function(qty)\\n\\t\\t\\tif qty == 0 and item.obj and not item.error then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tself:acceptObject(item.obj)\\n\\t\\t\\telse\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.log(\\\"#LIGHT_BLUE# Creating %d items:\\\", qty)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tDialog:yesnoPopup(_t\\\"Ego\\\", _t\\\"Add an ego enhancement if possible?\\\", function(ret)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif not ret then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor i = 1, qty do\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal n = game.zone:finishEntity(game.level, \\\"object\\\", item.e, {ego_chance=-1000})\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tn:identify(true)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.zone:addEntity(game.level, n, \\\"object\\\", self.actor.x, self.actor.y)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.log(\\\"#LIGHT_BLUE#Created %s\\\", n:getName({do_color=true}))\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tend\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q027\",\"source\":\"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared. Oh, take this. #LIGHT_GREEN#*He hands you a key*#WHITE# It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago. If you happen to find a text in the ruins entitled \\\"Inverted and Reverted Probabilistic Fields,\\\" return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically.\",\"target\":\"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。哦，带上这个。#LIGHT_GREEN#*他交给你一把钥匙。*#WHITE#它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。要是你在废墟之中找到一份标题是《反转与复原概率场》的文献，请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\",\"source_context\":\"\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"withheld_orb\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[Very well. There is no hurry. But I will need to spend a number of days studying it before we can create your portal.]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I understand. I'll return with the Athame and Diamond.\\\", action=function(npc, player) player:hasQuest(\\\"east-portal\\\"):setStatus(engine.Quest.COMPLETED, \\\"gotoreknor\\\") end},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\n---------------------------------------------------------------\\n-- back with materials\\n---------------------------------------------------------------\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"has_material_gave_orb\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"Thank you, and farewell.\\\", action=function(npc, player) player:hasQuest(\\\"east-portal\\\"):open_telmur(player) end},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"has_material_withheld_orb\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[Excellent. Are you yet willing to leave the Orb in my care for a time?]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I dare not let it out of my sight. I'm sorry.\\\", jump=\\\"no_orb_loan\\\"},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"Here it is. Guard it carefully. I must return to the Far East soon.\\\", jump=\\\"orb_loan\\\"},\\n\\t}\\n}\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q028\",\"source\":\"@playername@, you are called to serve. The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\\nYou must go there and find the source.\",\"target\":\"@playername@，你效力的时候到了。附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\\n你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\",\"source_context\":\"-- This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\\n-- but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\\n-- MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\\n-- GNU General Public License for more details.\\n--\\n-- You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\\n-- along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.\\n--\\n-- Nicolas Casalini \\\"DarkGod\\\"\\n-- darkgod@te4.org\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"welcome\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I will, Grand Keeper.\\\", action=function() game:changeLevel(1, \\\"unhallowed-morass\\\") end},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"I am sorry, but I cannot do that.\\\", action=function(npc, player) player:setQuestStatus(\\\"start-point-zero\\\", engine.Quest.FAILED) end},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nreturn \\\"welcome\\\"\\n\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q029\",\"source\":\"#{bold}#Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain#{normal}#\\nNothing but hatchlings so far. Honestly, if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon, let alone cover our losses. I've really spared no expense this time as well: Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know, and Sodelost... his prices are exorbitant, but then what else would you expect from those money-grubbing dwarven Thronesmen? I must admit I don't know much about Xann. The locals say there's no finer wyrmic in the area, and I admit she is something special in combat. Now, if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\",\"target\":\"#{bold}#探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽#{normal}#\\n到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。老实说，照这样下去，我们得到的龙皮连一条龙都盖不住，更别说弥补损失了。这次我也确实不惜血本：高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一；至于苏达罗斯特……他的要价高得离谱，不过钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人还能是什么样？我得承认，自己并不了解希安。当地人说这一带没有比她更出色的龙战士，而她在战斗中确实不同凡响。现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\",\"source_context\":\"--\\n-- Nicolas Casalini \\\"DarkGod\\\"\\n-- darkgod@te4.org\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n-- The Daikara\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nnewLore{\\n\\tid = \\\"daikara-note-1\\\",\\n\\tcategory = \\\"daikara\\\",\\n\\tname = _t\\\"expedition journal entry (daikara)\\\",\\n\\tlore = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n}\\n\\nnewLore{\\n\\tid = \\\"daikara-note-2\\\",\\n\\tcategory = \\\"daikara\\\",\\n\\tname = _t\\\"expedition journal entry (daikara)\\\",\\n\\tlore = _t[[#{bold}#Sodelost, Dwarf Rogue#{normal}#\\nCan't believe I agreed to this expedition. I suppose it's because I've known Relle for a while. We've crossed paths many times at Derth's trading post. I even gave her a special rate for my services. Sentimental fool! All it's got me is boots filled with snow and a light coinpurse. I still don't understand why these Kingdom types are so enamoured with drakeskin... makes superior armour they say. Pah! If you can't handle metal armour, what business do you have even wearing armour? Leather has about as much use as a halfling tied to a... noises up ahead, must stop writing.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewLore{\\n\\tid = \\\"daikara-note-3\\\",\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q030\",\"source\":\"Report for bad behavior\",\"target\":\"举报我的不良行为\",\"source_context\":\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tend\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tend\\n\\t\\t\\tend\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tif citem and citem.login then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal data = profile.chat:getUserInfo(citem.login)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif data then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal list = {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{name=_t\\\"Show infos\\\", ui=\\\"show\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{name=_t\\\"Whisper\\\", ui=\\\"whisper\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{name=_t\\\"Ignore\\\", ui=\\\"ignore\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{name=_t\\\"Open profile(in browser)\\\", ui=\\\"profile\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t{name=_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", ui=\\\"report\\\"}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif data.char_link then table.insert(list, 3, {name=_t\\\"Open charsheet(in browser)\\\", ui=\\\"charsheet\\\"}) end\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tDialog:listPopup((\\\"User: \\\"):tformat(citem.login), _t\\\"Action\\\", list, 300, 200, function(sel)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif not sel or not sel.ui then return end\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif sel.ui == \\\"show\\\" then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal UserInfo = require \\\"engine.dialogs.UserInfo\\\"\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tgame:registerDialog(UserInfo.new(data))\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\telseif sel.ui == \\\"profile\\\" then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tutil.browserOpenUrl(data.profile, {is_external=true})\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\telseif sel.ui == \\\"charsheet\\\" then\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tutil.browserOpenUrl(data.char_link, {is_external=true})\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\telseif sel.ui == \\\"whisper\\\" then\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q031\",\"source\":\"Place the object where?\",\"target\":\"将物品丢弃到哪里？\",\"source_context\":\"\\t\\tgame:registerDialog(self)\\n\\tend)\\n\\tcoroutine.resume(co)\\nend\\n\\n--- Create the object, either dropping it or adding it to the player or npc's inventory\\nfunction _M:acceptObject(obj, actor)\\n\\tif not obj then game.log(\\\"#LIGHT_BLUE#No object to create\\\")\\n\\telse\\n\\t\\tobj = obj:cloneFull()\\n\\t\\tactor = actor or self.actor or game.player\\n\\t\\t-- choose where to put object (default is current actor's inventory)\\n\\t\\tlocal d = Dialog:multiButtonPopup(_t\\\"Place Object\\\", _t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\t{{name=(\\\"Inventory of %s%s\\\"):tformat( actor:getName(), actor.player and _t\\\" #LIGHT_GREEN#(player)#LAST#\\\" or \\\"\\\"), choice=\\\"player\\\", fct=function(sel)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t-- if not obj.quest and not obj.plot then obj.__transmo = true end\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tactor:addObject(actor.INVEN_INVEN, obj)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.zone:addEntity(game.level, obj, \\\"object\\\")\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t_M.findObject(self, obj, actor)\\n\\t\\t\\tend},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name=(\\\"Drop @ (%s, %s)%s\\\"):tformat(actor.x, actor.y, actor.player and _t\\\" #LIGHT_GREEN#(player)#LAST#\\\" or \\\"\\\"), choice=\\\"drop\\\", fct=function(sel)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.zone:addEntity(game.level, obj, \\\"object\\\", actor.x, actor.y)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tgame.log(\\\"#LIGHT_BLUE#Dropped %s at (%d, %d)\\\", obj:getName({do_color=true}), actor.x, actor.y)\\n\\t\\t\\tend},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name=(\\\"NPC Inventory\\\"):tformat(), choice=\\\"npc\\\", fct=function(sel)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal x, y, act = _M.objectToTarget(self, obj)\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q032\",\"source\":\"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\",\"target\":\"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\",\"source_context\":\"\\timage = \\\"object/money_large.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Amassed 1000 gold pieces.]],\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who)\\n\\t\\treturn who.money >= 1000\\n\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"object/money_large.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who)\\n\\t\\treturn who.money >= 3000\\n\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{ id = \\\"DRAGON_GREED\\\",\\n\\tname = \\\"Dragon's Greed\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"object/money_large.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]],\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who)\\n\\t\\treturn who.money >= 8000\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q033\",\"source\":\"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\",\"target\":\"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\",\"source_context\":\"\\tdesc = _t[[Got to wave 20 in the arena.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Arena Battler 50\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Got to wave 50 in the arena.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Almost Master of Arena\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Master of Arena\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Became the new master of the arena in 60-wave mode.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"XXX the Destroyer\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Earned the rank of Destroyer in the arena.]],\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q034\",\"source\":\"I will not let you down!\",\"target\":\"我一定会让你失望的！\",\"source_context\":\"-- MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\\n-- GNU General Public License for more details.\\n--\\n-- You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\\n-- along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.\\n--\\n-- Nicolas Casalini \\\"DarkGod\\\"\\n-- darkgod@te4.org\\n\\nnewChat{ id=\\\"welcome\\\",\\n\\ttext = _t[[I do not have time to talk. This ritual is intense, and we are not alone here. Stop them!]],\\n\\tanswers = {\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\"},\\n\\t\\t{_t\\\"[leave]\\\"},\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\n\\nreturn \\\"welcome\\\"\\n\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q035\",\"source\":\"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\",\"target\":\"竞技场生存至第20轮。\",\"source_context\":\"\\tdesc = _t[[Unlocked Arena mode.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Arena Battler 20\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Got to wave 20 in the arena.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Arena Battler 50\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Almost Master of Arena\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.]],\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Master of Arena\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Became the new master of the arena in 60-wave mode.]],\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q036\",\"source\":\"Now, this is impressive!\",\"target\":\"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"source_context\":\"\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"You know who's to blame (reprise)\\\", id = \\\"FIRST_BOSS_MYSSIL\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"npc/humanoid_halfling_protector_myssil.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed Myssil, causing her to drop the Rod of Recall.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"LINANIIL_DEAD\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"npc/humanoid_human_linaniil_supreme_archmage.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Fear of Fours\\\", id = \\\"SLIME_TUNNEL_BOSSES\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed all four bosses of the Slime Tunnels.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who, target)\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q037\",\"source\":\"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\",\"target\":\"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\",\"source_context\":\"\\tname = \\\"Cryomancer\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Unlocked Archmage class and did over one million cold damage (with any item/talent/class).]],\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\",\\n\\tmode = \\\"world\\\",\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who, dam)\\n\\t\\tself.nb = (self.nb or 0) + dam\\n\\t\\treturn self.nb > 1000000 and profile.mod.allow_build.mage\\n\\tend,\\n\\ttrack = function(self) return tstring{tostring(math.floor(self.nb or 0)),\\\" / 1000000\\\"} end,\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Lichform\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Best album ever!\\\", id = \\\"THE_CURE\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.]],\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", \\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who)\\n\\t\\tself.nb = (self.nb or 0) + 1\\n\\t\\tif self.nb >= 89 then return true end\\n\\tend,\\n\\ttrack = function(self) return tstring{tostring(self.nb or 0),\\\" / 89\\\"} end,\\n}\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q038\",\"source\":\"Kickin' it old-school\",\"target\":\"现代风格\",\"source_context\":\"\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"I'm a cool hero\\\", id = \\\"NO_DERTH_DEATH\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"npc/humanoid_human_human_farmer.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Saved Derth without a single inhabitant dying.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"FIRST_BOSS_URKIS\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"npc/humanoid_human_urkis__the_high_tempest.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed Urkis, the Tempest, causing him to drop the Rod of Recall.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Leave the big boys alone\\\", id = \\\"FIRST_BOSS_MASTER\\\",\\n\\timage = \\\"npc/the_master.png\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed The Master, causing him to drop the Rod of Recall.]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q039\",\"source\":\"Killed a boss while already dead.\",\"target\":\"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\",\"source_context\":\"\\t\\t\\treturn true\\n\\t\\tend\\n\\tend,\\n\\ton_gain = function(_, src, personal)\\n--\\t\\tgame:setAllowedBuild(\\\"construct\\\")\\n--\\t\\tgame:setAllowedBuild(\\\"construct_runic_golem\\\", true)\\n\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Take you with me\\\", id = \\\"BOSS_REVENGE\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n\\tmode = \\\"player\\\",\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who, target)\\n\\t\\tlocal p = game.party:findMember{main=true}\\n\\t\\tif target.rank >= 3.5 and p.dead then\\n\\t\\t\\treturn true\\n\\t\\tend\\n\\tend,\\n}\\n\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Look at me, I'm playing a roguelike!\\\", id = \\\"SELF_CENTERED\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q040\",\"source\":\"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\",\"target\":\"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\",\"source_context\":\"\\tname = \\\"Paradoxology\\\", id = \\\"PARADOX_FULL\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Both killed your future self and got killed by your future self.]],\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Explorer\\\", id = \\\"EXPLORER\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Used the Sher'Tul fortress exploratory farportal at least 7 times with the same character.]],\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Orbituary\\\", id = \\\"ABASHED_EXPANSE\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]],\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Wibbly Wobbly Timey Wimey Stuff\\\", id = \\\"UNHALLOWED_MORASS\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"name\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Killed the weaver queen and the temporal defiler.]],\\n}\\nnewAchievement{\\n\\tname = \\\"Matrix style!\\\", id = \\\"ABASHED_EXPANSE_NO_BLAST\\\",\\n\\tshow = \\\"full\\\", huge=true,\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Finished the whole Abashed Expanse zone without being hit by a single void blast or manaworm. Dodging's fun!]],\\n\\tcan_gain = function(self, who, zone)\\n\\t\\tif not who:isQuestStatus(\\\"start-archmage\\\", engine.Quest.DONE) then return false end\"}]}"}],"timestamp":1787984354405},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze each item.\n\nQ021: source: \"which you do not understand: #{italic}#...\" target: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：...\" Source says \"which you do not understand\" — target says \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" (\"even if you know this language, you cannot understand\"). That's a negation flip. Source: you do not understand. Target: even if you know this language, you cannot understand. Hmm, source_context: the lore branch when player does NOT speak shertul shows \"which you do not understand:\" followed by the untranslated text; when speaks_shertul, shows translation. The source string is the \"which you do not understand\" variant. Target adds \"即使你懂得这种语言\" — actually this inverts: source states player doesn't understand; target says even if you know the language you cannot understand. This is a negation/condition defect. FINDING, CONDITION or STATE. Evidence: \"which you do not understand\". target_span: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". Correction: \"你看不懂：\" or similar. Actually source says \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand\" — the text underneath which you do not understand. Correction: \"下面有一些你看不懂的文字：\". FINDING, CONDITION (negation flipped). Claim_type: CONDITION or STATE. Use CONDITION.\n\nWait—but the source_context shows the two branches: untranslated text shown when player does NOT speak shertul, translated when does. The target's \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" contradicts: source's branch shows the untranslated string precisely because you don't understand. Actually target says even if you know the language you can't understand it — the string \"Sho ch'zun...\" is shertul language, untranslated. In source, \"which you do not understand\" is the correct meaning. Target changes to \"even if you understand this language, you cannot understand\" — flip. FINDING.\n\nQ022: source: \"The staff will allow us to drain...\" target: \"这根法杖将让我们得以...\" OK. Source context has \"The staff has allowed us\" but the source given says \"will allow\". Translation matches source \"will allow\" — 将让我们得以. Fine. Also last line: \"You cannot stop us now!\" → \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — \"You cannot stop us now\" means \"你们现在无法阻止我们\" (you are unable to stop us). Target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了\" — same meaning. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ023: source: \"What do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\" target: \"你想干什么，@playerdescriptor.race@？\" Fine. The italic part: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" → \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\" — \"peer out\" = 向外窥视/望出来. Target says \"凝视着他\" — at him? Source doesn't specify object. \"peer out\" — looking out through the slot. \"凝视着他\" adds \"him\" — could be the NPC peering out at the player. Minor addition but compatible with context (the NPC peers out at the player who's at the door). \"gaze at him\" — the player is the one addressed; the eyes peer out at... the player. But target uses \"他\" (him) while the addressee is the player (\"你\"). Also \"A slot in the door opens\" → \"门上开了一个小洞\" — slot = 狭缝/小口, \"小洞\" is a hole, minor. \"凝视着他\" vs \"向外窥视\" — the pronoun 他 refers to whom? If the eyes belong to the doorkeeper, they peer out at the player, so should be \"你\" or just \"向外张望\". Is this an objective defect? The \"him\" as referent is wrong-ish—the addressee is the player addressed as \"你\". But it could refer to a third person present. Hmm. It's a mild referent issue. I'd report as UNCERTAIN maybe. Actually rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence isn't a defect. The peering is at whoever is at the door; in the dialog the player. Using 他 while addressing 你 is inconsistent but possibly a translation convention. I'll report UNCERTAIN for REFERENT? Or skip. Also \"peer out\" means to look out from within; \"凝视着他\" adds a direction. I think it's low severity; I might report UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Hmm, let me be careful about false positives. The main sentence is fine. I'll leave candidates empty for Q023? The \"他\" is the most questionable. The dialog is between NPC and player; eyes peer out and look at the player (\"你\"). Translating as \"他\" introduces third-person referent not in source. I'd report as FINDING? It's fairly subjective. I'll do UNCERTAIN with REFERENT.\n\nQ024: \"Aeryn, are you well?\" → \"艾琳，你还好么？\" Fine. No defect.\n\nQ025: source: \"Thanks, my lady. I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\" target: \"谢谢，我的女士。我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\" Fine. \"orbs of command\" → 指令水晶球 — okay, orb = 球. Fine. No defect.\n\nQ026: \"Number of items to make\" → \"制作的物品数量\" Fine.\n\nQ027: source: \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" target: \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Hmm \"and I'll have everything prepared\" — future: \"我就会把一切都准备好\". Target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" adds certainty, and \"准备好了\" perfective. Minor. Actually \"I'll have everything prepared\" = 届时我会把一切都准备好. Target is close. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as \"I will surely have everything ready\" — acceptable. Second: \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago.\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。\" Fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率。\" — \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\" — our attempt to create the portal / portal attempt. Target says \"你通过传送门时\" (when you pass through the portal). Source: \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt at the portal (creating/opening portal). Hmm — \"surviving our portal attempt\" — could be surviving the attempt to open the portal. Target shifts to surviving passing through the portal. Is that a defect? \"our portal attempt\" is ambiguous; the risk is during the portal creation/travel. The target changes \"our\" to \"你\" and \"attempt\" to \"通过传送门时\". This changes subject: our attempt → your passing through. I'd report as FINDING? It's arguably ambiguous. \"our portal attempt\" — the attempt involving the portal they will create for the player. \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\" = your odds of surviving when you go through the portal. Source: your odds of surviving our attempt at the portal. These differ: whose action. \"our\" vs \"your\". I'd report FINDING with SUBJECT/OTHER? Or UNCERTAIN. Hmm. The safest: report UNCERTAIN with claim OTHER or SUBJECT. Evidence: \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\". target_span: \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Correction: \"我们尝试开启传送门时你存活的几率\" or \"你在我们尝试传送时存活的几率\". I'll mark FINDING? The change of \"our\" to \"你\" is objective. But \"portal attempt\" could mean \"attempt to use the portal\" — still \"our attempt\". The target removes \"our\". I'll do UNCERTAIN.\n\nActually also \"Return in a few days\" — 几天后你回来 fine.\n\nQ028: source: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" fine. \"The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless.\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动。\" fine. \"You must go there and find the source.\" → \"你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头。\" \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" adds \"这一切的\" — minor addition, compatible. Fine.\n\nQ029: source: \"Relle, Cornac Fighter & Expedition Captain\" → \"探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽\" fine. \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" Hmm — \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" means: so far we've only encountered hatchlings (nothing but = only). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings — that's the OPPOSITE! Source: only hatchlings (no adult dragons). Target: never met hatchlings. That's a clear negation flip / value error. FINDING. Evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" target_span: \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\"。 Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到过幼龙\". Claim_type: OTHER or VALUE/STATE. Use STATE? It's about what they've encountered. I'd use VALUE or STATE. Let's use STATE.\n\nWait — could \"Nothing but hatchlings\" mean \"nothing except hatchlings\" i.e., only hatchlings so far — yes. And the rest: \"if this keeps up we won't have enough dragonhide to cover a dragon\" — consistent with only finding hatchlings (not enough dragonhide). Target \"从未遇上幼龙\" contradicts. Definitely FINDING.\n\nAlso \"Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know\" → \"高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座那群贪财的矮人\" — \"money-grubbing\" included as 贪财, Thronesmen → 钢铁王座 (Throne). Fine. \"Xann\" → 希安. \"wyrmic\" → 龙战士 — wyrmic is a class; 龙战士 acceptable. \"if only she could turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons!\" → \"现在只盼她能把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙！\" — \"draconic talents\" → 操控龙族力量的本事 — addition but compatible. Fine.\n\nSo Q029 has one FINDING.\n\nQ030: source: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — \"my\" is added; source is a menu action to report a user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" = report MY bad behavior — wrong direction! It should be \"举报不良行为\" (report [them] for bad behavior). Adding \"我的\" reverses the meaning. FINDING. Evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\". target_span \"举报我的不良行为\". Correction: \"举报不良行为\". Claim_type: SUBJECT or DIRECTION. Use SUBJECT? Or ADDITION. I'd say SUBJECT (who did bad behavior). Or DIRECTION. I'll use SUBJECT.\n\nQ031: source: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" ≠ \"丢弃\" (drop). The popup offers both inventory and drop options, so \"放置\" is correct; \"丢弃\" narrows to drop. FINDING. Evidence: \"Place the object where?\" target_span \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\". Claim_type: ACTION. Note source_context shows options include \"Inventory of %s\" and \"Drop @\" — supporting that place ≠ only drop. That context supports the finding.\n\nQ032: source: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" target: \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" — target adds \"在'龙之贪婪'成就中\". From source_context, the achievement with 3000 is \"Treasure Hoarder\"; Dragon's Greed is 8000. So the addition is wrong info — it attaches the desc to Dragon's Greed achievement, but 3000 corresponds to Treasure Hoarder. However, the rule: addition compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong by evidence? The context shows DRAGON_GREED desc = 8000. So adding \"在龙之贪婪成就中\" to a 3000 desc is contradicted by visible evidence. FINDING. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" for DRAGON_GREED, and the 3000 desc belongs to \"Treasure Hoarder\". Evidence must be verbatim from source_context: I can quote \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" and \"return who.money >= 3000\". Evidence string should be verbatim occurrence. I'll use: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" ... hmm evidence must be a single verbatim string. Use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — verbatim in context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` yes. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim_type: ADDITION.\n\nQ033: \"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\" → \"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\" Fine. Note in context this is \"Almost Master of Arena\" but translation only handles desc; fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite! \"let you down\" = 让你失望; \"I will NOT let you down\" = 我不会让你失望. Target says \"我一定会让你失望的\" = I will definitely disappoint you. FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"I will not let you down!\" Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\".\n\nQ035: source: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" target: \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20. FINDING, VALUE. Evidence: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" Correction: \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\"\n\nQ036: source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" target: \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" but compatible-ish. Source is an achievement name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — actually from context it's an achievement name for killing Linaniil. Adding \"发现\" — hmm, is that judgeable wrong? Source: \"Now, this is impressive!\" — \"这可真令人印象深刻！\" Target adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). The achievement is about a kill, not a discovery. But by visible evidence alone, \"this discovery\" is an addition that specifies the referent as a discovery. Is it \"compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong\"? The context desc: \"Killed Linaniil...\" — killing isn't a discovery. Hmm, achievements can be named loosely. I think this is a mild addition. Could report UNCERTAIN ADDITION. Actually rule: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" The evidence shows the achievement is for killing Linaniil — \"这个发现\" (this discovery) is arguably incompatible... but the exclamation could refer to anything. I lean UNCERTAIN or empty. Hmm. I'll report UNCERTAIN with ADDITION: target adds \"发现\" which is not in source; the source is a general exclamation. Actually is it worth reporting? It's a name; adding \"发现\" changes meaning somewhat. I'll include UNCERTAIN.\n\nHmm, but caution against over-reporting. The exclamation \"Now, this is impressive!\" in context of killing — the target invents a discovery. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: source: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" target: \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — \"power\" (力量) is omitted; \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" = 对力量与永生的狂热梦想. Target: \"成就你的野心\" (achieved your ambition) — \"power\" dropped, \"wild\" dropped. OMISSION of \"power\". Is it substantive? \"dreams of power and eternal life\" → 野心 covers dreams generally but loses \"power\". Also \"eternal life\" kept. Hmm — \"野心\" (ambition) loosely covers \"power and eternal life\" dreams? It only explicitly mentions eternal life. Omission of \"力量\". Report FINDING OMISSION? It's a partial omission; the meaning \"wild dreams of power\" is fairly significant for a Lichform achievement. I'd report FINDING OMISSION with evidence \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" and correction \"实现了你对力量与永生的狂想：你成为了巫妖！\". Or UNCERTAIN. \"野心\" does encompass desire for power arguably... but combined with only 永恒的生命 mentioned. I'll do FINDING? Hmm. Let me think: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — the target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\" reads as: achieved your ambition AND obtained eternal life. Actually that covers both power (ambition) and eternal life. \"野心\" ≈ ambition for power. It's a reasonable compression. I'd say no objective defect... but \"wild\" omitted, minor. I'll leave empty. Hmm, borderline. I'll leave empty candidates for Q037.\n\nQ038: source: \"Kickin' it old-school\" target: \"现代风格\" — completely opposite! \"old-school\" = 老派/复古; target says 现代风格 (modern style). FINDING, DIRECTION or VALUE. Evidence: \"Kickin' it old-school\". Correction: \"老派风格\" / \"怀旧复古\". Claim_type: DIRECTION (opposite meaning) or OTHER. Use DIRECTION? It's more VALUE (wrong style). I'll use OTHER or DIRECTION. \"old-school\" → modern is an antonym flip: DIRECTION.\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" — matches: the player (main) is dead and kills a boss (BOSS_REVENGE \"Take you with me\"). Fine. p.dead means the main party member is dead. Target fine.\n\nQ040: source: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" target: \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"maintain it in orbit\" = 维持其轨道运行; target says \"稳定在地面上\" (stabilize on the ground) — opposite/orbit omitted. Also \"Abashed Expanse\" translated as 次元浮岛 (a known translation? The zone is a floating shard). The key defect: \"in orbit\" → \"在地面上\". FINDING. Evidence: \"maintain it in orbit\". target_span: \"使其稳定在地面上\". Correction: \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\". Claim_type: VALUE or STATE. Use STATE? \"in orbit\" vs \"on the ground\" — VALUE/STATE. I'll use STATE.\n\nNow double-check Q022 for any issue: source \"The staff will allow us\" — context has \"has allowed\" for one branch; but source given is \"will allow\", target matches. Also \"You cannot stop us now!\" target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" — good. Context's alternate has \"It is already too late...\" — not relevant. No findings for Q022.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ028: fine. Actually \"unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" — restless = 烦躁不安/躁动; 蠢蠢欲动 means about to move/start action — acceptable.\n\nQ030: confirm — the menu item is an action on another user in chat, \"Report for bad behavior\" — report that user for bad behavior. \"举报我的不良行为\" says report my own bad behavior — wrong. FINDING.\n\nQ031: FINDING.\n\nQ034: FINDING.\n\nQ035: FINDING.\n\nQ038: FINDING.\n\nQ040: FINDING.\n\nQ021: FINDING.\n\nQ029: FINDING.\n\nQ032: FINDING.\n\nQ027: UNCERTAIN for \"our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时\". Let me finalize. Also check \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" — \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future; \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads fine as future in Chinese (\"到时候肯定准备好了\"). OK.\n\nQ023: I'll include the UNCERTAIN REFERENT for \"凝视着他\". Hmm, actually reconsider: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" — peer out = 向外窥视. Target \"凝视着他\" — the \"他\" refers presumably to the player, but the next line addresses the player as \"你\". Within the same text, \"他\" would be confusing. But is this a \"客观、实质性\" defect? The peering direction and object are added. I'll include UNCERTAIN REFERENT. Evidence: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\". target_span: \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\"。\n\nActually wait — the player is @playerdescriptor.race@, being addressed. The eyes peer out at the player. Using 他 vs 你 — in Chinese game translations, third person for the player is odd but occurs. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ036: UNCERTAIN ADDITION: \"这个发现\" — the source is just an exclamation; the achievement (per context) is for killing Linaniil, not a discovery. I'll make it FINDING? Evidence: \"name = \\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", id = \\\"LINANIIL_DEAD\\\"\" and desc \"Killed Linaniil\" — but evidence field must be verbatim from source or source_context. I could use \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\" as evidence showing it's a kill not a discovery. Hmm, but the translation is of the name \"Now, this is impressive!\" — the name itself doesn't mention discovery. Adding \"这个发现\" specifies a referent that conflicts with the kill context. I'd say UNCERTAIN is safer. Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\". Correction: \"这可真令人印象深刻！\". Verdict UNCERTAIN, claim ADDITION.\n\nHmm, actually reconsider whether to report Q036 at all. \"Now, this is impressive!\" as an achievement name for killing the Supreme Archmage — \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻\" — \"发现\" is a genuine addition not supported. I'll keep UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ027 finalize: UNCERTAIN, claim SUBJECT or OTHER. \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\" → \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". Changes \"our portal attempt\" (our attempt at the portal) to \"when you pass through the portal\". Whose action changed: our → your passing. I'd claim SUBJECT. target_span \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\". evidence \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\". Correction: \"这能大大提高你在我们尝试开启传送门时的存活几率。\" Verdict: UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ037: decide. \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — target \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\". \"power\" — 野心 implies ambition which in context = power? Not explicit. \"wild\" omitted. Hmm. Two components: power + eternal life. Target: 野心 (ambition — could cover power) + 永恒的生命. I think this is a defensible compression; not an objective defect. Empty.\n\nActually wait, one more consideration for Q021: the target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" — could the translator have intended a different meaning from source? Source: \"There is some text underneath which you do not understand:\" — the translation flips it to \"even if you know this language, you cannot understand it\". Given source_context, the untranslated text is shown when the player does NOT speak shertul — so \"you do not understand\" is correct; target's version is a different claim. This is an objective change. FINDING, claim CONDITION (negation of condition). target_span \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". evidence \"which you do not understand\". Correction: \"下面是一些你看不懂的文字：\" — well the target only needs correcting the clause: \"你看不懂：\". Correction: \"你看不懂这种语言：\". I'll write correction as \"你看不懂：\" plus keep rest.\n\nNow output JSON with 20 items Q021–Q040 in order, each with observation. Observations in Chinese, brief.\n\nSchema minItems 20 maxItems 20 — exactly 20.\n\nWrite candidates arrays:\n\nQ021: [{FINDING, CONDITION, \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\", \"你看不懂这种语言：\", \"which you do not understand\"}]\n\nQ022: []\n\nQ023: [{UNCERTAIN, REFERENT, \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\", \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\", \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}]\n\nQ024: []\n\nQ025: []\n\nQ026: []\n\nQ027: [{UNCERTAIN, SUBJECT, \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\", \"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\", \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}]\n\nQ028: []\n\nQ029: [{FINDING, STATE, \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\", \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\", \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}]\n\nQ030: [{FINDING, SUBJECT, \"举报我的不良行为\", \"举报不良行为\", \"Report for bad behavior\"}]\n\nQ031: [{FINDING, ACTION, \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\", \"将物品放置到哪里？\", \"Place the object where?\"}]\n\nQ032: [{FINDING, ADDITION, \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\", \"积累3000金币。\", \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}] — hmm, target_span must appear verbatim in target: target is \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — target_span \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\" — appears (without the final 。). Yes. Evidence verbatim from source_context: `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` — yes appears. But maybe better evidence: the desc for Dragon's Greed is 8000. The finding: the 3000 desc is attached to wrong achievement name. Evidence could be \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" plus id DRAGON_GREED. I'll use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — shows 3000 desc belongs to Treasure Hoarder (its desc is the SOURCE_MATCH). Actually the SOURCE_MATCH_1 is in the Treasure Hoarder block: desc = _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]], with can_gain who.money >= 3000. So evidence \"return who.money >= 3000\" also good. Use both? Only one evidence string allowed. I'll use `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",`. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" claim ADDITION.\n\nQ033: []\n\nQ034: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"我一定会让你失望的！\", \"我不会让你失望的！\", \"I will not let you down!\"}]\n\nQ035: [{FINDING, VALUE, \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\", \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\", \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}]\n\nQ036: [{UNCERTAIN, ADDITION, \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"这可真是令人印象深刻！\", \"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}]\n\nQ037: []\n\nQ038: [{FINDING, DIRECTION, \"现代风格\", \"老派风格\", \"Kickin' it old-school\"}]\n\nQ039: []\n\nQ040: [{FINDING, STATE, \"使其稳定在地面上\", \"使其稳定维持在轨道上\", \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}]\n\nObservations: brief Chinese descriptions. For empty candidates, observation like \"译文与原文语义一致，未发现可报告的客观缺陷。\"\n\nCheck Q040 claim type: \"in orbit\" vs \"在地面上\" — that's a location/state error; STATE fine.\n\nQ029 STATE fine, or VALUE. Keep STATE.\n\nQ038 DIRECTION (opposite). fine.\n\nQ021 CONDITION fine.\n\nWrite the JSON now. Must be pure JSON, no markdown.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"items\":[{\"neutral_id\":\"Q021\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"CONDITION\",\"target_span\":\"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\",\"correction\":\"你看不懂这种语言：\",\"evidence\":\"which you do not understand\"}],\"observation\":\"原文陈述'你看不懂下面的文字'，译文改为'即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解'，否定了原文条件含义；source_context 显示该未翻译文本仅在玩家不懂 Sher'Tul 语时显示，进一步支持原义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q022\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文与原文语义一致，'will allow' 对应'将让我们得以'，'You cannot stop us now' 对应'你现在已经无法阻止我们了'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q023\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"REFERENT\",\"target_span\":\"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\",\"correction\":\"一双狂乱的眼睛向外窥视\",\"evidence\":\"a pair of wild eyes peer out\"}],\"observation\":\"原文'peer out'只表示向外窥视，未指明对象；译文增加'凝视着他'，且下文以'你'称呼对话者，'他'的指代与可见证据的关系存在歧义。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q024\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"译文准确对应原文'你还好么'，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q025\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'没能找到所有的指令水晶球'与 'have not been able to find all of the orbs of command' 语义一致，请求部分亦对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q026\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'制作的物品数量'为 'Number of items to make' 的准确对应，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q027\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"你通过传送门时存活的几率\",\"correction\":\"这能大大提高你在我们进行传送门尝试时的存活几率\",\"evidence\":\"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\"}],\"observation\":\"原文说'我们（our）的传送门尝试'，译文改为'你通过传送门时'，动作主体与场景有所偏移，但'portal attempt'本身略有歧义，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q028\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'你效力的时候到了'对应 'you are called to serve'，其余部分对应良好；'这一切的源头'为与证据相容的少量补充，不构成缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q029\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\",\"correction\":\"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\",\"evidence\":\"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Nothing but hatchlings' 意为'到目前为止只有幼龙'，译文'从未遇上幼龙'含义相反，且与后文'龙皮不够'的逻辑矛盾。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q030\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"SUBJECT\",\"target_span\":\"举报我的不良行为\",\"correction\":\"举报不良行为\",\"evidence\":\"Report for bad behavior\"}],\"observation\":\"这是对其他用户操作的菜单项，原文无'我的'；译文加入'我的'后变成举报自己的不良行为，主体指向错误。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q031\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ACTION\",\"target_span\":\"将物品丢弃到哪里？\",\"correction\":\"将物品放置到哪里？\",\"evidence\":\"Place the object where?\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'Place' 为中性'放置'，source_context 显示选项包含放入背包与丢弃两种；译文'丢弃'把动作窄化为丢弃之一，与选项集合不符。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q032\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\",\"correction\":\"积累3000金币。\",\"evidence\":\"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\"}],\"observation\":\"原文仅为'Amassed 3000 gold pieces.'；译文附加'在“龙之贪婪”成就中'，而 source_context 显示该描述属于 'Treasure Hoarder'（3000金币），Dragon's Greed 的描述为8000金币，新增信息与可见证据冲突。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q033\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰'与原文一致，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q034\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"我一定会让你失望的！\",\"correction\":\"我不会让你失望的！\",\"evidence\":\"I will not let you down!\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'I will not let you down' 为否定（不会让你失望），译文'我一定会让你失望的'含义完全相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q035\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"VALUE\",\"target_span\":\"竞技场生存至第20轮。\",\"correction\":\"竞技场生存至第50轮。\",\"evidence\":\"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为第50波，译文写为第20轮，数值错误；source_context 中第20波属于另一成就 'Arena Battler 20'。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q036\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"claim_type\":\"ADDITION\",\"target_span\":\"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"correction\":\"这可真是令人印象深刻！\",\"evidence\":\"desc = _t[[Killed Linaniil, the Supreme Archmage of Angolwen.]]\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为泛指的感叹'Now, this is impressive!'，译文添加'这个发现'；结合 source_context 该成就对应击杀事件而非发现，新增指涉与证据存在张力，但成就名可作宽松修辞，故列为 UNCERTAIN。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q037\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命'可视为对 'wild dreams of power and eternal life' 的压缩表达，力量含义由'野心'承载，未构成可客观判定的实质性缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q038\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"DIRECTION\",\"target_span\":\"现代风格\",\"correction\":\"老派风格\",\"evidence\":\"Kickin' it old-school\"}],\"observation\":\"原文 'old-school' 意为老派、复古，译文'现代风格'含义相反。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q039\",\"candidates\":[],\"observation\":\"'在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS'与 'Killed a boss while already dead' 语义一致，source_context 中 can_gain 判定亦相符，未发现客观缺陷。\"},{\"neutral_id\":\"Q040\",\"candidates\":[{\"verdict\":\"FINDING\",\"claim_type\":\"STATE\",\"target_span\":\"使其稳定在地面上\",\"correction\":\"使其稳定维持在轨道上\",\"evidence\":\"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\"}],\"observation\":\"原文为'maintain it in orbit'（维持其轨道运行），译文'稳定在地面上'与轨道状态相悖。\"}]}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai-standard-cn","model":"glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":8920,"output":7825,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6270,"totalTokens":16745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cach